+# M01 Halfway Checkpoint
+
+The citation and convention audit is complete. Ben-Itzhak--Teicher Theorem
+3.4 applies to identity factorizations into transpositions of the same length.
+Its move `(a,b)->(aba^{-1},a)` is the inverse of the project's named right
+move `(a,b)->(b,b^{-1}ab)`, hence the orbit relation is identical.
+
+The key closure observation is stronger and simpler than the manuscript's
+proof sketch: within each labeled weighted component one may explicitly build
+an identity representative consisting entirely of adjacent equal pairs. The
+classification connects the original word to that representative. Every one
+of its pairs can then be refreshed, using an exact length-four heat bath, to a
+single fixed transposition. This connects every state to the same universal
+word.
+
+Remaining at this checkpoint: write the boundary-window realization and all
