# Resolution Ledger: Local Heat-Bath Polynomial Mixing

STATUS: ACTIVE
STRONGEST RESULT: Qualitative irreducibility of K, J, and every nonempty arbitrary-endpoint aligned-H4 bridge is proved. The m=4 gap is at least 1/4; K dominates B by 1/12 and J by 1/(3 binom(N,2)^2). Long B bridges reduce with constant-per-scale loss to arbitrary-endpoint pair bridges of length O(N log N); the pair-length-three base gap M^-16 is independently accepted, and pair length four has a coordinator-audited 2/(3M^20) bound pending fresh review. The audited macro projection dominates square down-up S by 1/[24(m-2)]; dense support partitions, color projections, all one-gate modes, and square-deletion action rates have inverse-polynomial bounds. Full macro restrictions are polynomially controlled by their connected-Hurwitz-coordinate gaps through an independently accepted shuttle flow.
SMALLEST OPEN IMPLICATION: Prove BASE-SCALE FIXED-ENDPOINT GAP uniformly for every feasible microfactorized Q bridge of pair length O(N log N); qualitative irreducibility and fixed pair lengths two and three are now closed, but their state-count bounds do not have a length-independent exponent. This base theorem would give a universal B gap and hence Terminal A through K>=B/12. Alternative open routes are a connected-Hurwitz gap plus the remaining macro allocation/projection bounds, or an explicit infinite superpolynomial-gap obstruction for K. Nonirreducibility is ruled out.
ACTIVE ASSIGNMENTS: Cycle 04 wave 2: fresh M14 l=4 theorem/general-bound referee; all-length crude bridge baseline plus counterexample lane; fresh M10 probability referee plus quantitative-Hurwitz resource continuation; coordinator non-hub zipper/integration lane.
