codex
The optimized exact harness is now working and has already sharpened the conjecture: through \(n=5\), every ideal parking exchange has an actual path of length at most two, and the worst single-path capacity loss is only \(1/3\). I’m scaling this to \(n=8\); it is a falsifier, not a proof, but it is now testing the precise flow inequality rather than mere reachability.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'python3 experiments/20260811-polynomial-mixing-resolution/cycle-08/mission-M39-parking-two-hop-falsifier/exact_two_hop.py --n-max 8 --output experiments/20260811-polynomial-mixing-resolution/cycle-08/mission-M39-parking-two-hop-falsifier/results.json' in /home/nico/projects/research_projects/reversible_circuits
