### L-0114 - Mesoscopic literal disconnected-macro shells are not bottlenecks

M33 extends the exact full-chain shell rejection from logarithmic to
mesoscopic radius. For `N>=10^6`, `m=4N^3+4`, and every

    1<=a<=floor(N log(N+1)/100),

the literal graph-distance shell `V^(a)` around all disconnected words obeys

    pi(V^(a))<=exp(-4N^2),
    Phi_pm^K(V^(a))>=N^-25.

The proof shrinks overlapping update clusters to their first and last cut
crossings, keeps exact `m^c/c!` layout entropy, and matches it by explicit
two-crossing excursion sources. Distinct excursion prefix states force any
subgroup-valued interval to contain whole consecutive pairs, ruling out
three-crossing regrouping. Robust identity skeletons handle every alternate
cut. One genuine `H_5` surgery exits the exact shell; all scan, fiber, and
laziness factors are charged and unused flow remains nonnegative.

Thus shell radius divided by `log N` tends to infinity without producing a
Terminal-B cut. The remaining enumerative loss is
`(M/binom(N-1,2))^(4a)=exp(O(a/N))`, so the next scale is quadratic.

