We will make use of the notion of total positivity of order 2.

Definition 3.3. Let A = (Ai,j)i,j≥0 be an array of nonnegative numbers. It is said
to be totally positive of order 2 (TP2), if all its 2 × 2 minors are non-negative,
that is for all i ≤ i′ and all j ≤ j′, we have Ai,jAi′,j′ ≥ Ai,j′Ai′,j.

Proposition 3.4 below states the well-known fact that the Toeplitz matrix of a
log-concave sequence is TP2.

