# Resolution Ledger: Local Heat-Bath Polynomial Mixing

STATUS: ACTIVE
STRONGEST RESULT: Qualitative irreducibility of K, J, and every nonempty arbitrary-endpoint aligned-H4 bridge is proved. The m=4 gap is at least 1/4; K dominates B by 1/12 and J by 1/(3 binom(N,2)^2). Independently audited bridge reductions show that one base length R_N=O(N log N) controls every longer Hamiltonian with loss at most 4(R_N-1); pair lengths three and four have independently accepted gaps M^-16 and 2/(3M^20). An exact leave-one-coordinate recursion reduces the complete-pair bridge gap to a normal coordinate-correlation Gram operator with O(N^4) active range, and pointwise smoothing bounds its retention norm by 5/(4l) above C_mix N log(N+1). Microfiber coordinate modes have exact retention 1/l. In the minimal long-cycle sector every fixed parking-multiset restriction has an inverse-polynomial gap. An independently audited Lorentzian clone down-up chain on the parking-multiset projection has gap at least 1/r; a canonical comparison reduces it to adjacent-value ideal moves with gap at least r^-7. The audited macro projection dominates square down-up S by 1/[24(m-2)]; dense support partitions, color projections, all one-gate modes, and square-deletion action rates have inverse-polynomial bounds. Full macro restrictions are polynomially controlled by their connected-Hurwitz-coordinate gaps through an independently accepted shuttle flow. On the refutation side, for N>=10^12 and m=4N^3+4 every literal disconnected-macro neighborhood through radius floor(m/10^4) has conductance at least N^-25; the smaller m/10^8 theorem has independently passed a fresh referee. An overlap-heavy removable-leaf union in the minimal connected macro has conductance at least 1/(576N^3).
SMALLEST OPEN IMPLICATION: Prove PRODUCT-INCREMENT BASE CORRELATION below the pointwise-mixing scale, equivalently BASE-SCALE FIXED-ENDPOINT GAP uniformly through pair length O(N log N). Cyclic braid covariance reduces the coordinate-retention spectrum to scalar Toeplitz blocks, the dense tail has the required O(1/l) bound, and all fiber-centered coordinate directions are exactly controlled; the N-dependent product-increment interval remains open. Within the minimal long-cycle stratum the remaining exact implication is ADJACENT-VALUE PARKING FLOW: route the adjacent-value ideal chain, whose gap is at least r^-7, through the stationary-flow projection of the actual rank-two heat bath with polynomial total congestion. Exact enumeration refutes length-two routing at r=5 for unrestricted ideal moves, and an adjacent-value family refutes uniform two-hop capacity; longer distributed routes remain open. The complete-pair route has an audited polynomial local-to-complete comparison. A base theorem would give a universal B gap and hence Terminal A through K>=B/12. Alternative open routes are a connected-Hurwitz gap plus the remaining macro allocation/projection bounds, or an explicit infinite superpolynomial-gap obstruction for K. Nonirreducibility is ruled out.
ACTIVE ASSIGNMENTS: Cycle 11: M35 adjacent-value parking flow and universal leaf-rotation count; M44 weighted-Dyck quartile or full-K bottleneck red team; M46 fresh leaf-rotation referee and auxiliary-chain counterexample specialist; M41 coordinator Cayley-lift and adjacent-flow comparison.
