### L-0141 - M35 freezes the universal leaf-rotation theorem

For a parking macro interpreted as a preorder plane-tree degree sequence,
let leaf `j` be a nonlast child of `i`.  M35 proves by interval-component
structure and the Goulden--Yong contraction/insertion bijection that the
actual projected rank-two heat bath contains the rotation

    m -> m-e_i+e_j

with exact forward and reverse probabilities

    2m_i/[3r(r-1)]  and  2/[3r(r-1)].

The proof counts `m_i |O_m|/r` marked sources and retains the corrected
`3(r-1)` scan/heat-bath normalization.  Exact contraction and insertion
checks pass through `n=7`.  Together with the already proved comparison, the
adjacent-value ideal chain has gap at least `r^-7`; however a universal
two-hop comparison is rigorously false and longer distributed leaf-rotation
flows remain open.

M35 also checks that Fleurat's log-concave simply-generated-tree growth
theorem applies to `w_k=1/k!`.  Time reversal supplies the exact aggregate
weighted deletion balance, but the infinite-support proof is compactness
based and supplies no pointwise polynomial transition bound.  A weighted
canonical-flow argument may use aggregate balance, but still needs a
polynomial load estimate and an exact comparison from deletion/replanting to
the parking leaf rotation.

