Python and NumPy versions, the multiplication convention, and the universal
claim each finite computation can falsify.

## 9. Verdict

OPEN AT A NAMED STEP: BASE-SCALE CGL ACCUMULATION (5.1).

The deletion recursion, normal scalar Gram reduction, and dense-tail lemma
are proved.  The naive product from l=2 and the sharp coefficient-one
candidate mu_l<=1/(l-1) are refuted.  What remains is the accumulated
correlation or exceptional-mode gap through
3<=l<C_mix N log(N+1).  This is a nonterminal proof reduction.

