## 3. Probability, runtime, path, and congestion accounting

- C_(l,h) chooses each of binom(l,2) raw pairs with coefficient
  1/binom(l,2); the leave-one-out identity (2.1) has the exact factor 1/l.
- A_(l,h) chooses each single-coordinate sigma-field with coefficient 1/l.
- The braid deletion is a deterministic measure-preserving bijection of
  length at most l-1.  It is used only for exact conjugacy of conditional
  kernels, not as a comparison flow, so there is no path congestion.
- The dense pointwise error is 1/(64l).  Four density factors give at most
  4epsilon/(1-epsilon)^2<=1/(4l), and the l-by-l Gram sum gives
  mu_l<5/(4l).
- The finite group harness uses exact integer convolution counts followed by
  deterministic floating diagonalization of an O(lN^4) product Gram matrix.
  It has no random seed.  The scalable identity-mode harness uses p(N)
  partitions and exact big-integer character/branching formulas; the full
  N<=40 grid ran in approximately 11 seconds in Python 3.12.3.
- No canonical paths, randomized routing, or congestion estimates enter the
  proved recursion or dense-tail theorem.

## 4. Dependencies, labeled

- PROVED HERE: the micro-Hurwitz deletion intertwining in the left-boundary
  convention, including straddling pairs; recursion (1.1); comparison (2.2);
  Gram identity; central marginal laws; cyclic covariance; normality; scalar
  spectrum; exceptional-mode dichotomy; and identity character/branching
  formulas (2.19)-(2.21).
- CITED AND HYPOTHESES CHECKED: Diaconis--Shahshahani, Generating a Random
  Permutation with Random Transpositions, Lemma 14 and the Section 3
  partition-zone bounds, for the fixed-error pointwise estimate.  The
  parity conversion and 1/l amplification are rederived in Section 2.5.
- CITED FOR METHOD ONLY: Carlen--Geronimo--Loss, Determination of the
  Spectral Gap in the Kac Model for Physical Momentum and Energy Conserving
  Collisions, Lemmas 3.1 and 4.1.  The finite-dimensional statements used
  here are proved directly.
- INHERITED PROVED: the exact N=6 rational three-site Rayleigh certificate;
  aligned arbitrary-endpoint bridge connectivity; and accepted fixed-length
  l=2,3,4 gap bounds.  Only the rational certificate is needed for the
  refutation in Section 2.4.
- EMPIRICAL/FINITE: floating all-endpoint spectra through N=8.  They are used
  only to falsify candidates and test universal algebraic identities.
- EXACT FINITE, NOT ASYMPTOTIC: the integer character/branching grid through
  N=40.  Exactness of each entry does not make the observed scaling a proof.
- OPEN: every uniform accumulated base-scale bound below
  C_mix N log(N+1).

