Summing for `1<=k<=r-1` gives `2 floor(r^2/4)`, proving (1.5).

If an update stays in `F_N` but crosses from `A_q` to its complement, its old
state must lie in `q-delta_r<Area<=q`.  For a fixed `r`, averaging over the
