notes/local-heatbath-polynomial-mixing-resolution-resolution-ledger.md:5:SMALLEST OPEN IMPLICATION: Prove PRODUCT-INCREMENT BASE CORRELATION below the pointwise-mixing scale, equivalently BASE-SCALE FIXED-ENDPOINT GAP uniformly through pair length O(N log N). Cyclic braid covariance reduces the coordinate-retention spectrum to scalar Toeplitz blocks, the dense tail has the required O(1/l) bound, and all fiber-centered coordinate directions are exactly controlled; the N-dependent product-increment interval remains open. Within the minimal long-cycle stratum, ROOT-MEAN LIFT is now reduced exactly to SPINE-BIAS H-minus-one BOUND: the sum of the squared dual norms of all shape-dependent right-spine split biases, divided by their quotient rates, must be polynomial in r. This would close FULL ACTUAL PARKING FLOW because the quotient has gap 2/[9e r(r-1)] and the exact child restrictions leave a 1/(9r) induction margin. The restricted leaf-rotation comparison has an independently checked reversible-pebbling obstruction and is no longer a viable standalone route. The complete-pair route has an audited polynomial local-to-complete comparison. A base theorem would give a universal B gap and hence Terminal A through K>=B/12. Alternative open routes are a connected-Hurwitz gap plus the remaining macro allocation/projection bounds, or an explicit infinite superpolynomial-gap obstruction for K. Nonirreducibility is ruled out.
