# Contextual branch-local reduction for the spine-bias functional

Date: 2026-08-11.  This note concerns the full nonlazy minimal-sector
parking projection `Pbar_r`.  It is not a statement about the identity
bridge chain `K`.

## 1. Contextual locality theorem

Fix a coarse root composition `b=(c_1,...,c_k)` and a one-split refinement
`a` obtained by replacing `c_i` by `(A,B)`.  A state in the coarse fibre is
an ordered tuple of independent local branch macros

```text
d=(u_1,...,u_k),  u_j in J_(c_j-1).
```

Write `p_(b,a)(d)=Pbar_r(d,F_a)`.

**Theorem 1 (contextual split locality).**  For fixed `(r,b,a,i)`, there is
a function
> `phi_(r,b,a,i)` on `J_(c_i-1)` such that
> ```text
> p_(b,a)(d)=alpha_r phi_(r,b,a,i)(u_i).             (1.1)
> ```

### Proof

Let `I_j` be the preorder interval of root branch `j`.  In the noncrossing
factor tree, all edges of this branch lie in `{0} union I_j`, and there is
exactly one edge from `0` into `I_j`.  Restrict a numbered chord diagram to
those edges, close the factor-number gaps, and standardize `I_j`.  The
Goulden--Yong clockwise inequalities are preserved.  The accepted
sufficiency theorem therefore identifies the restriction as a minimal
factorization on `c_j+1` vertices whose root degree is one and whose
nonroot local macro is `u_j`.

Conversely, take one such root-unary local factorization for each branch.
Their chord diagrams occupy disjoint cyclic intervals and meet only at
`0`.  Shuffle their factor orders while preserving each local order and
requiring the `k` distinguished root-attachment factors to appear in the
reverse of the root-child order.  Local clockwise inequalities remain
valid, and the displayed order is exactly the only new inequality at
`0`.  Goulden--Yong sufficiency gives a unique global factorization with
root composition `b`.  Restriction and union are inverse.  This proves the
root-branch constrained-shuffle bijection.

For a fixed local macro `u_j`, its local root-unary orbit has size

```text
|O^+_(u_j)|=c_j!/product_(v in I_j)d_v!.             (1.2)
```

Its lower-label multiset contains exactly one zero.  Stanley--Biane says
that every permutation of that multiset occurs once, so the distinguished
root-attachment factor occupies each of the `c_j` local word positions in
exactly

```text
|O^+_(u_j)|/c_j                                      (1.3)
```

local words.  In particular this position law is independent of the shape
and degree multiplicities inside the branch.

A transition from `b` to the fixed refinement `a` uses a pair consisting
of branch `i`'s root-attachment factor and one factor in the same local
diagram.  Cutting the resulting last-child suffix subtree is the universal
right-spine support theorem.  Record the local word, the local positions of
the pair, and one favourable rank-two outcome.  A global shuffle realizes
this marked transition precisely when it leaves the two marked local
factors consecutive and puts every distinguished root factor in the
required order.  For fixed local positions, the number of such shuffles
depends only on `(r,b,i)` and those positions, not on any local chord shape.

Now fix the marked local word in branch `i` and sum the extensions over all
local words in every branch `j!=i`.  Equation (1.3) shows that this number
is

```text
[product_(j!=i)|O^+_(u_j)|] times
a combinatorial factor depending only on (r,b,i) and the marked positions.
                                                               (1.4)
```

On the other hand the unrestricted orbit size is

```text
|O_d|=r!/[k! product_v d_v!]
     ={r!/[k! product_j c_j!]}
       product_j |O^+_(u_j)|.                       (1.5)
```

Divide the marked favourable-outcome count by
`3(r-1)|O_d|`, the exact pair-fibre, scan, and source-orbit normalization.
All factors involving `u_j`, `j!=i`, cancel between (1.4) and (1.5).
What remains is a weighted sum over marked local words of branch `i`, with
weights determined by `(r,b,a,i)` and their local positions.  It is a
function only of `u_i`.  Dividing by the fixed `alpha_r` defines `phi` and
proves (1.1).  The argument counts ordered favourable outcomes, so it does
not lose a factor when a pair has two macro-identical outcomes.  QED

The exact audit independently finds no fixed `(b,a,i,u_i)` collision through
`r=7` and no contextual-versus-unary support mismatch.

A stronger scalar reduction to the unary-root split function is false.
Even for fixed `(b,a,i)`, the ratio between the contextual normalized rate
and the unary normalized rate varies with `u_i`; the exact `r=7` report has
many such failures.  Across all positive tested entries the ratio ranges
from `1/5` to `2`, but this finite range is not a universal bound.

## 2. Exact H-minus consequence

Put

```text
s=c_i-1,
gamma_i=s(s-1)/[r(r-1)],
bar phi=E_(pi_s) phi.
```

The M50 product restriction gives

```text
pi(.|b)=tensor_j pi_(c_j-1),
E_b=sum_j gamma_j E_(Pbar_(c_j-1)).                 (2.1)
```

The bias functional is

```text
ell_(b,a)(g)=alpha_r E[(phi(u_i)-bar phi)g].         (2.2)
```

Conditional expectation over every coordinate other than `i` preserves
(2.2) and cannot increase (2.1).  Conversely a local test function attains
the local dual supremum.  Hence

```text
||ell_(b,a)||_(-1,b)^2
 =alpha_r^2/gamma_i
   ||phi-bar phi||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2.                   (2.3)
```

Since `q_(b,a)=alpha_r bar phi` and

```text
alpha_r/gamma_i=2/[3s(s-1)]=alpha_s,                (2.4)
```

division gives

```text
||ell_(b,a)||_(-1,b)^2/q_(b,a)
 =alpha_s ||phi-bar phi||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2/bar phi.    (2.5)
```

Equivalently, if `p^ctx_s=alpha_s phi`, the right side is exactly

```text
||p^ctx_s-E p^ctx_s||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2/E p^ctx_s.      (2.6)
```

Thus the global normalization cancels completely: no factor depending on
`r` is lost in passing to the split branch.  This is the effective-resistance
form in which a recursive proof could be additive rather than multiplying a
Radon--Nikodym loss at every depth.

For `s<=1` the local fibre is a singleton and both sides vanish, so (2.3)
has the natural zero convention rather than a division by `s(s-1)`.

## 3. Why this does not yet prove the target

The contextual local observable `phi` is not a scalar multiple of the
ordinary unary split observable, and no universal shuffle formula has been
proved which converts its position-weighted marked sum to an already bounded
coboundary.  Consequently (2.6) is a full-chain dual norm of a contextual
rate function, not one of the already bounded quotient modes.  Bounding it
by the unknown full spectral gap is circular and loses the powers needed by
the balanced induction.

The smallest surviving constructive proposition is therefore:

> **CONTEXTUAL SPINE COBOUNDARY.**  Construct, for every position-weighted
> contextual rate `p^ctx_s` produced by Theorem 1, an internal `Pbar_s`
> flow routing
> `pi_s(p^ctx_s-Ep^ctx_s)` with energy at most
> `s^C E p^ctx_s`; the sums over all contextual splits must obey the same
> polynomial bound.

Together with (2.3)--(2.6), this proposition proves M54's SPINE-BIAS
H-minus-one BOUND.  The exact audit can refute locality or a proposed
uniform ratio, but its passes cannot prove this proposition.
# Exact marked-history density recurrence

Date: 2026-08-11.  Write `P=Pbar_r`,
`alpha=2/[3r(r-1)]`, and let `L_k={d in J_r:d_0=k}`.  Let `pi_k` be
`pi_r` conditioned on `L_k`.  The exact root-degree law is

```text
p_k=pi_r(L_k)
   =binom(r-1,k-1) r^(r-k)/(r+1)^(r-1), 1<=k<=r.    (1.1)
```

## 1. Canonical and random-boundary kernels

For `x in L_k`, let `M_k(x,y)` retain only moves that merge the first two
root branches.  M50 gives total rate `alpha k` for that boundary, so

```text
M_k(x,y)=P(x,y)/(alpha k)                            (1.2)
```

on its support.  This is a stochastic kernel from `L_k` to `L_(k-1)`.
The uniform-boundary variant retains every root-decreasing move and has

```text
Mtilde_k(x,y)=P(x,y)/[alpha k(k-1)].                 (1.3)
```

Iterating either kernel until `L_1` is the marked coalescence map.

## 2. Exact reverse-history recurrence

Let `eta_k` be the unnormalized distribution in layer `k` after all original
states with root degree at least `k` have been coalesced down to that layer.
Thus

```text
eta_r=p_r pi_r,
eta_(k-1)=p_(k-1)pi_(k-1)+eta_k M_k.                (2.1)
```

Put `h_k=d eta_k/d pi_k`.  Reversibility gives the exact pointwise
recurrence

```text
h_r=p_r,
h_(k-1)(y)=p_(k-1)
 +[p_(k-1)/(p_k alpha k)]
   sum_(x in L_k:first-merge(x)=y) P(y,x)h_k(x).     (2.2)
```

For the uniform-boundary schedule, replace `alpha k` by
`alpha k(k-1)` and sum over every `x in L_k` adjacent to `y`.

At `k=1`, `eta_1` has total mass one, so `g_r=h_1` is exactly the
Radon--Nikodym density of the endpoint law with respect to `pi_1`.  Equivalently,
for the canonical schedule,

```text
g_r(y)=p_1 sum_(reverse first-split histories from y)
             product_(layer k step) P(x_(k-1),x_k)/(alpha k).  (2.3)
```

The zero-step history gives the universal pointwise lower bound

```text
g_r(y)>=p_1=(r/(r+1))^(r-1)>=e^(-1).                (2.4)
```

Formula (2.3) is the requested valid ordered-cut-history partition
function.  Its nonzero terms are shape-dependent.

## 3. Exact failure of stationary normalization

At the smallest nontrivial case `r=3`, start in root composition `(1,2)`
with its stationary conditional law and merge its only boundary.  The
output and stationary target laws on the unary-root macros are

```text
macro                 output       pi(. | root composition (3))
(0,1,1)                  0                       1/3
(0,1,2)                  1                       2/3.
```

The density is therefore `0,3/2`.  The star-under-the-root target has no
valid right-spine cut of the required ordered sizes.  Marking the cut makes
the bijection exact, but forgetting the mark does not give the stationary
coarse-fiber law.

Mixing over every initial root degree softens but does not remove the bias.
At `r=3`, canonical coalescence has endpoint densities `15/16,33/32` and
total variation `1/48`; uniform-boundary coalescence has densities
`57/64,135/128`.

## 4. Exact finite L2 diagnostics

The bounded audit gives the following endpoint chi-square divergences from
`pi_1`:

```text
r       2          3          4          5          6          7
canonical
        0       .001953    .007494    .013191    .018295    .022713
uniform boundary
        0       .005981    .013141    .019619    .025157    .029839
```

The exact rational values and extremizers are in `marked_history_n8.json`.
Canonical pointwise density through `r=7` lies between approximately
`.6994` and `1.3262`; the extreme low state is the unary root above a star.
These finite values are compatible with small aggregate distortion but do
not prove any asymptotic bound.

## 5. Surviving proposition

> **MARKED-HISTORY L2 CONTROL.**  Prove an exact bound on the recurrence
> (2.2) strong enough that its endpoint and prefix occupation densities
> incur only a multiplicative `1+O(1/r)` loss in the recursive all-pairs
> flow (an `O(1/r)` chi-square bound is a candidate), and prove that the
> resulting edge loads are additive/polynomial rather than a constant loss
> multiplied once per depth.

A constant pointwise bound at one recursion level is not sufficient:
raising a fixed constant through depth `Theta(r)` is exponential.  The
recurrence (2.2), rather than the product of the crude one-step Radon bounds,
is the smallest exact object that must be controlled.

## 6. Factorially weighted nested-split partition

There is a useful cancellation which is not visible in (2.2).  Let
`y_1 in L_1`, and let

```text
y_1 <- y_2 <- ... <- y_k
```

be a reverse canonical history: `y_l in L_l`, and `y_l -> y_(l-1)` is
the forward merge of the first two root branches.  Put

```text
a_l(y_(l-1),y_l)=P(y_(l-1),y_l)/alpha.              (6.1)
```

If the reverse split removes a degree unit from a vertex whose degree in
`y_(l-1)` is `q_l`, then

```text
pi(y_l)/pi(y_(l-1))=q_l/l.                          (6.2)
```

Detailed balance and the forward normalization `alpha l` give

```text
[pi(y_l)/pi(y_(l-1))]
 [P(y_l,y_(l-1))/(alpha l)]
 =P(y_(l-1),y_l)/(alpha l)=a_l/l.                   (6.3)
```

Therefore, if `H_s(y)` is the total product of the `a_l` weights over all
length-`s` nested reverse histories from `y`, with `H_0=1`, then the exact
endpoint density is

```text
g_r(y)=p_1 sum_(s=0)^(r-1) H_s(y)/(s+1)!.           (6.4)
```

Every reverse step cuts a last-child suffix subtree from the current first
root branch; all previously cut branches remain an ordered root suffix.
Thus (6.4) is literally a nested right-spine suffix-cut partition function,
not merely an algebraic path sum.

Its first moments are explicit.  The mass supplied by initial layer
`L_(s+1)` is `p_(s+1)`, so

```text
E_(pi_1) H_s=(s+1)! p_(s+1)/p_1
 = (s+1)! binom(r-1,s)/r^s <=s+1.                   (6.5)
```

Equations (6.4)--(6.5) are universal consequences of reversibility and the
accepted M50 boundary normalization.  The exact probe checks both identities
without a failure through `r=7`.

## 7. Two tempting bounds and the corrected sufficient condition

The individual canonical reverse first-split bound

```text
P(y,x)<=alpha                                         (7.1)
```

has no exact counterexample through `r=7`, but remains unproved.  More
importantly, the literal harmonic bound on the total first-split propensity
is false.  At global `r=5`,

```text
y=(0,0,1,2,3),  root composition (4,1),
sum_(canonical first refinements x) P(y,x)/alpha=13/6>H_4=25/12.  (7.2)
```

Even in the unary layer it first fails at tested `r=7`:

```text
y=(0,1,1,3,4,5,6),
sum_x P(y,x)/alpha=157/60=H_7+1/42.                 (7.3)
```

Thus neither `H_(first branch size)` nor `H_r` may be cited as proved.
The following robust replacement would still yield polynomial endpoint
density:

> **LOGARITHMIC NESTED-SPLIT PROPENSITY.**  There is a universal `C` such
> that, in every layer and every suffix context,
> `sum_x P(y,x)/alpha <= C log(r+1)` over canonical first refinements.

Indeed the recursive definition of `H_s` would give

```text
H_s(y)<=[C log(r+1)]^s,
g_r(y)<=p_1 exp(C log(r+1))<=(r+1)^C.               (7.4)
```

This proves only polynomial endpoint `L-infinity`, hence polynomial `L2`;
it does not by itself make recursive edge loads additive.  Exact values
through `r=7` are compatible with the logarithmic replacement, but finite
agreement is not evidence for the universal inequality.

## 8. Alignment with the stronger H-minus frontier

M54 gives the sharper sufficient functional **SPINE-BIAS H-minus-one
BOUND**.  Endpoint control in (6.4) is one possible way to build its
effective-resistance flow, but the literal task is now to prove

```text
sum_(a refining b) ||ell_(b,a)||_(-1,b)^2/q_(b,a)
 <= A r^C.                                           (8.1)
```

The exact nested identity does not prove (8.1): first moments (6.5) do not
control pairs of histories or their internal edge occupation.  A valid next
step must bound the two-history intersection/effective-resistance term, not
multiply one-step Radon maxima.

