 <=(r+1)(e/D)^D,
```

proving (8.1).  In particular, for

```text
D_r=2+ceil(log_2(r-1)),
```

the right side is superpolynomially small: for every fixed `C`, it is
`o(r^-C)`.

This turns the proposed reversible-pebbling invariant into a precise cut
