# Exact full-Pbar root-composition projection and its polynomial gap

Date: 2026-08-11.  Permutations compose as `(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`, and
factor tuples multiply left-to-right.  This theorem concerns the full
nonlazy adjacent rank-two projection `Pbar_r` in the minimal factorization
sector of `(0 1 ... r)`.  It is not a theorem for the original identity
chain `K`.

## 1. Statement

For `r>=2`, let

```text
J_r={d in N^r:sum_i d_i=r and sum_(i=0)^q d_i>=q+1},
pi_r(d)=r!/[(r+1)^(r-1) product_i d_i!].
```

Append `d_r=0` and let `T(d)` be the unique rooted plane tree with preorder
outdegrees `(d_0,...,d_r)`.  Its root children have ordered branch sizes

```text
a(d)=(a_1,...,a_k),   a_i>=1,   sum_i a_i=r,   k=d_0,
```

where a branch size includes its root edge.  Let `Rroot_r` be the
stationary-flow projection of `Pbar_r` under `d -> a(d)`.

Put

```text
Z_s=(s+1)^(s-1)/s!,  Z_0=1,
w_a=Z_(a-1)=a^(a-1)/a!  for a>=1,
alpha_r=2/[3r(r-1)].
```

**Theorem 1 (root-composition projection).**  The stationary law of `Rroot_r`
on ordered compositions of `r` is

```text
rho_r(a_1,...,a_k)
 = [1/Z_r] [1/k!] product_i w_(a_i).                 (1.1)
```

For every adjacent pair `a_p,a_(p+1)`, let `a^merge` replace them by their
sum.  Then the exact two rates are

```text
Rroot_r(a,a^merge)=alpha_r k,                        (1.2)
Rroot_r(a^merge,a)=alpha_r
   w_(a_p)w_(a_(p+1))/w_(a_p+a_(p+1)).              (1.3)
```

Moreover, with the singleton convention at `r=1`,

```text
gap(Rroot_r) >= 2/[9 e r(r-1)]                      (1.4)
```

for every `r>=2`.

The projection in this statement is a stationary-flow projection.  It is
not claimed to be a strong lumping of `Pbar_r`.  Indeed reverse split rates
from two degree trees having the same coarse root composition can differ;
the smallest exact witness is given in Section 5.

## 2. Full-move child-boundary lemma

For a vertex `h` of `T(d)`, let its `k=d_h` child-subtree intervals be
`I_1,...,I_k` from left to right.  For every `p<k`, consider all upward
`Pbar_r` transitions generated by a word-adjacent pair of lower-`h`
factors corresponding to the attachment edges of `I_p,I_(p+1)`.

**Lemma 2.1 (exact boundary rate).**  For every `d,h,p` as above, the sum
of the rates of all those transitions is

```text
2d_h/[3r(r-1)].                                      (2.1)
```

Every such transition changes `d` to `d-e_h+e_j`, where `j` lies in
`I_p`; geometrically it merges child branches `p,p+1` by attaching the
second somewhere along the right spine of the first.  Every upward
off-diagonal transition belongs to exactly one such child boundary.

**Proof.**  Let `O_d` be the minimal long-cycle words with degree vector
`d`.  Stanley--Biane identifies `O_d` with all permutations of the parking
multiset having `d_h` copies of `h`, so

```text
|O_d|=r!/product_h d_h!.
```

The canonical interval-component lemma from M35 says that the factor chord
tree has exactly one edge from `h` into each `I_q`.  These are precisely the
factors whose lower endpoint is `h`.  Goulden--Yong clockwise-decreasing
factor labels put those `d_h` edges in the reverse of the child-interval
order when they are read in word order.  Thus a fixed consecutive pair of
occurrences among the lower-`h` factors is exactly a fixed adjacent child
boundary.

In a uniformly random permutation of a multiset of length `r` with `d_h`
copies of `h`, the gaps before, between, and after those copies are a
uniform weak composition of `r-d_h` into `d_h+1` parts.  A specified
internal gap is zero with probability

```text
binom(r-1,d_h-1)/binom(r,d_h)=d_h/r.
```

Consequently a fixed child boundary contributes exactly

```text
d_h |O_d|/r                                          (2.2)
```

marked source words and scan positions.

Write the corresponding ordered factor pair as

```text
(h,b)(h,j),   h<j<b,
```

where the second edge attaches the earlier child interval.  Its ordered
product has exactly the three decompositions

```text
(h,b)(h,j),  (h,j)(j,b),  (j,b)(h,b).
```

Both noncurrent outcomes, and only those, replace one lower label `h` by
`j`.  The interval order gives `j in I_p`.  The target preorder degree word
is feasible.  Immediately before the first vertex of `I_(p+1)` is read, the
open-vertex stack inside `I_p` consists exactly of the right spine of
`I_p`; decreasing `d_h` and increasing `d_j` keeps the preorder stack valid
exactly when `j` is one of those open vertices.  Thus the unique target plane
tree is obtained by merging the two branches and attaching `I_(p+1)` along
that right spine.  Dividing
(2.2) by `|O_d|`, then by the `r-1` scan sites and the three fibre outcomes,
and multiplying by the two favorable outcomes proves (2.1).

Conversely, every upward macro transition starts from an adjacent pair of
equal lower labels.  The two factors are two consecutive lower-`h`
attachment edges, hence determine one child boundary.  QED

Taking `h=0` in Lemma 2.1 gives (1.2), pointwise for every degree tree in a
fixed refined root composition.  If `h>0`, both endpoints lie in the same
root branch and the root composition is unchanged.

## 3. Stationary law and reverse normalization

The simply-generated weight of a plane tree is

```text
omega(t)=product_v 1/d_v(t)!,   sum_(t:|t|=s) omega(t)=Z_s.
```

Fix a root composition `a=(a_1,...,a_k)`.  The root contributes `1/k!`,
and after deleting the root edge of branch `i`, its remaining subtree has
`a_i-1` edges and total weight `Z_(a_i-1)=w_(a_i)`.  This proves (1.1).

If `a^merge` merges parts `A,B`, then

```text
rho_r(a)/rho_r(a^merge)=(1/k) w_A w_B/w_(A+B).       (3.1)
```

The stationary-flow projection is reversible.  Multiplying (1.2) by
(3.1) gives (1.3), with every factor `3r(r-1)` retained.

It is useful to record that the split factor is never superpolynomially
small.  Put `c=A+B`.  Then

```text
w_Aw_B/w_c
 = binom(c,A)(A/c)^A(B/c)^B c/(AB).                  (3.2)
```

The binomial probability at its integer mean is at least `1/(3sqrt(c))`,
and `AB<=c^2/4`, so

```text
w_Aw_B/w_c >= 4/(3c^(3/2)) >=4/(3r^(3/2)).          (3.3)
```

Thus every positive quotient split rate is at least
`8/[9r^(5/2)(r-1)]`.  Bound (3.3) is not needed for the sharper canonical
path proof below, but it calibrates the reverse normalization.

## 4. Canonical paths and exact basin accounting

From a composition `x=(x_1,...,x_q)`, repeatedly merge its first two parts
until reaching the one-part hub `H=(r)`.  For every ordered pair `x,y`, use
the path from `x` to `H` followed by the reverse of the path from `y` to
`H`.  Its length is at most `2(r-1)`.

Fix a merge edge

```text
s=(A,c_2,...,c_(ell+1)) -> (A+c_2,c_3,...,c_(ell+1)).
```

The sources whose first-merge path uses this edge are exactly

```text
(b_1,...,b_p,c_2,...,c_(ell+1)),
```

where `(b_1,...,b_p)` is an arbitrary ordered composition of `A`.  Define

```text
C_(A,p)=sum_(b_1+...+b_p=A) product_i w_(b_i).
```

The rooted-tree exponential generating function

```text
T(z)=sum_(a>=1) w_a z^a,   T(z)=z exp(T(z))
```

and Lagrange inversion give the exact identity

```text
C_(A,p)=[z^A]T(z)^p
       =p A^(A-p-1)/(A-p)!.                          (4.1)
```

Let `B_s` be the source basin of the edge.  Cancelling its fixed suffix in
(1.1) gives

```text
rho_r(B_s)/rho_r(s)
 =(ell+1)!/w_A sum_(p=1)^A C_(A,p)/(p+ell)!.
```

For every `p>=1`,

```text
(ell+1)!/(p+ell)! <=1/p!.
```

The root decomposition of all weighted plane trees with `A` edges says

```text
sum_(p=1)^A C_(A,p)/p!=Z_A.
```

Therefore

```text
rho_r(B_s)/rho_r(s)
 <=Z_A/w_A=Z_A/Z_(A-1)
 =(1+1/A)^(A-1)<=e.                                  (4.2)
```

This is the source-recovery and multiplicity accounting.  It is why the
one-part hub is harmless: it has stationary mass
`Z_(r-1)/Z_r=(r/(r+1))^(r-1)>=e^(-1)`, and the flow into every intermediate
edge has the local basin bound (4.2).

The stationary path length removes the extra worst-case factor `r`.  Put
`h(x)=number of parts of x minus one`.  Summing (1.1) over compositions of
fixed length, or equivalently using the root-degree law, gives

```text
h distributed as Bin(r-1,1/(r+1)),
E_rho h=(r-1)/(r+1)<1.                               (4.3)
```

Write the refined endpoint of a merge edge as
`s=(A,c_2,...,c_k)`, `k>=2`, and define its basin first moment

```text
M_s=sum_(x in B_s)rho_r(x)h(x).
```

The same fixed-suffix cancellation used above gives the exact formula

```text
M_s=rho_r(s)[k!/w_A]
    sum_p [(p+k-2)C_(A,p)/(p+k-1)!].                 (4.4)
```

For `p>=1,k>=2`,

```text
k!(p+k-2)/(p+k-1)! <=k/p!,                          (4.5)
```

because this is equivalent to
`p+k-2<=binom(p+k-1,p)`.  Equations (4.1)--(4.2) therefore give

```text
M_s<=e k rho_r(s).                                   (4.6)
```

Compare the one-step global `rho_r` heat bath, whose gap is one, to
`Rroot_r`.  For a commodity `(x,y)`, the path length is `h(x)+h(y)`.
The edge occurs in the first half exactly when `x in B_s` and in the second
half exactly when `y in B_s`; if both occur, both traversals are retained.
Thus its total length-weighted load is

```text
2[M_s+rho_r(B_s)E_rho h]
 <=2e(k+1)rho_r(s)
 <=3e k rho_r(s).                                    (4.7)
```

Its exact stationary capacity is

```text
Q_Rroot(s,s^merge)=rho_r(s) alpha_r k.               (4.8)
```

The congestion is at most `3e/alpha_r=9e r(r-1)/2`, proving (1.4).
This stationary-length sharpening was supplied in coordinator M41,
Section 11, from the exact formulas above and is rechecked here.  Every
route and every weight is computable in polynomial time; no exponentially
small canonical plane-tree shape is used.

## 5. Projection, not strong lumping

Forward merge rate (1.2) is pointwise independent of the internal branch
shapes.  Reverse split rates from an individual coarse degree tree need not
be independent of its shape, so `d -> a(d)` is not a strong lumping in both
directions.  At `r=3`, the two macros

```text
(0,1,1), (0,1,2)
```

both have coarse root composition `(3)`, but their total rates to refined
composition `(1,2)` are respectively `0` and `1/9`.  Stationary averaging
nevertheless gives the exact quotient split rate (1.3).  This distinction
prevents an unjustified Jensen mean-lift from the quotient back to full
`Pbar_r`.

For a fixed refined-to-coarse composition edge `a -> b`, the normalized
crossing flow has source marginal exactly `pi(.|a)`.  Its target marginal
`nu_(a,b)` satisfies

```text
d nu_(a,b)/d pi(.|b)
 =Pbar_r(d,F_a)/Rroot_r(b,a)
 <=1/Rroot_r(b,a)
 <=(9/8)r^(5/2)(r-1).                                (5.1)
```

Here the last inequality uses (1.3) and (3.3).  Thus the mean-lift bias is
polynomially absolutely continuous, but inserting (5.1) recursively at
every tree depth would multiply polynomial losses and does not by itself
prove a polynomial full gap.

## 6. Scope and exact falsification

The universal proof uses Stanley--Biane, the M35 interval-component lemma,
and the convention-checked Goulden--Yong incident-edge order.  The bounded
script `root_composition_audit.py` independently reconstructs every minimal
factorization, exact pair fibre, macro rate, plane tree, child boundary, and
root composition through `n=r+1<=8`.  It checks:
# Contextual branch-local reduction for the spine-bias functional

Date: 2026-08-11.  This note concerns the full nonlazy minimal-sector
parking projection `Pbar_r`.  It is not a statement about the identity
bridge chain `K`.

## 1. Contextual locality theorem

Fix a coarse root composition `b=(c_1,...,c_k)` and a one-split refinement
`a` obtained by replacing `c_i` by `(A,B)`.  A state in the coarse fibre is
an ordered tuple of independent local branch macros

```text
d=(u_1,...,u_k),  u_j in J_(c_j-1).
```

Write `p_(b,a)(d)=Pbar_r(d,F_a)`.

**Theorem 1 (contextual split locality).**  For fixed `(r,b,a,i)`, there is
a function
> `phi_(r,b,a,i)` on `J_(c_i-1)` such that
> ```text
> p_(b,a)(d)=alpha_r phi_(r,b,a,i)(u_i).             (1.1)
> ```

### Proof

Let `I_j` be the preorder interval of root branch `j`.  In the noncrossing
factor tree, all edges of this branch lie in `{0} union I_j`, and there is
exactly one edge from `0` into `I_j`.  Restrict a numbered chord diagram to
those edges, close the factor-number gaps, and standardize `I_j`.  The
Goulden--Yong clockwise inequalities are preserved.  The accepted
sufficiency theorem therefore identifies the restriction as a minimal
factorization on `c_j+1` vertices whose root degree is one and whose
nonroot local macro is `u_j`.

Conversely, take one such root-unary local factorization for each branch.
Their chord diagrams occupy disjoint cyclic intervals and meet only at
`0`.  Shuffle their factor orders while preserving each local order and
requiring the `k` distinguished root-attachment factors to appear in the
reverse of the root-child order.  Local clockwise inequalities remain
valid, and the displayed order is exactly the only new inequality at
`0`.  Goulden--Yong sufficiency gives a unique global factorization with
root composition `b`.  Restriction and union are inverse.  This proves the
root-branch constrained-shuffle bijection.

For a fixed local macro `u_j`, its local root-unary orbit has size

```text
|O^+_(u_j)|=c_j!/product_(v in I_j)d_v!.             (1.2)
```

Its lower-label multiset contains exactly one zero.  Stanley--Biane says
that every permutation of that multiset occurs once, so the distinguished
root-attachment factor occupies each of the `c_j` local word positions in
exactly

```text
|O^+_(u_j)|/c_j                                      (1.3)
```

local words.  In particular this position law is independent of the shape
and degree multiplicities inside the branch.

A transition from `b` to the fixed refinement `a` uses a pair consisting
of branch `i`'s root-attachment factor and one factor in the same local
diagram.  Cutting the resulting last-child suffix subtree is the universal
right-spine support theorem.  Record the local word, the local positions of
the pair, and one favourable rank-two outcome.  A global shuffle realizes
this marked transition precisely when it leaves the two marked local
factors consecutive and puts every distinguished root factor in the
required order.  For fixed local positions, the number of such shuffles
depends only on `(r,b,i)` and those positions, not on any local chord shape.

Now fix the marked local word in branch `i` and sum the extensions over all
local words in every branch `j!=i`.  Equation (1.3) shows that this number
is

```text
[product_(j!=i)|O^+_(u_j)|] times
a combinatorial factor depending only on (r,b,i) and the marked positions.
                                                               (1.4)
```

On the other hand the unrestricted orbit size is

```text
|O_d|=r!/[k! product_v d_v!]
     ={r!/[k! product_j c_j!]}
       product_j |O^+_(u_j)|.                       (1.5)
```

Divide the marked favourable-outcome count by
`3(r-1)|O_d|`, the exact pair-fibre, scan, and source-orbit normalization.
All factors involving `u_j`, `j!=i`, cancel between (1.4) and (1.5).
What remains is a weighted sum over marked local words of branch `i`, with
weights determined by `(r,b,a,i)` and their local positions.  It is a
function only of `u_i`.  Dividing by the fixed `alpha_r` defines `phi` and
proves (1.1).  The argument counts ordered favourable outcomes, so it does
not lose a factor when a pair has two macro-identical outcomes.  QED

The exact audit independently finds no fixed `(b,a,i,u_i)` collision through
`r=7` and no contextual-versus-unary support mismatch.

A stronger scalar reduction to the unary-root split function is false.
Even for fixed `(b,a,i)`, the ratio between the contextual normalized rate
and the unary normalized rate varies with `u_i`; the exact `r=7` report has
many such failures.  Across all positive tested entries the ratio ranges
from `1/5` to `2`, but this finite range is not a universal bound.

## 2. Exact H-minus consequence

Put

```text
s=c_i-1,
gamma_i=s(s-1)/[r(r-1)],
bar phi=E_(pi_s) phi.
```

The M50 product restriction gives

```text
pi(.|b)=tensor_j pi_(c_j-1),
E_b=sum_j gamma_j E_(Pbar_(c_j-1)).                 (2.1)
```

The bias functional is

```text
ell_(b,a)(g)=alpha_r E[(phi(u_i)-bar phi)g].         (2.2)
```

Conditional expectation over every coordinate other than `i` preserves
(2.2) and cannot increase (2.1).  Conversely a local test function attains
the local dual supremum.  Hence

```text
||ell_(b,a)||_(-1,b)^2
 =alpha_r^2/gamma_i
   ||phi-bar phi||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2.                   (2.3)
```

Since `q_(b,a)=alpha_r bar phi` and

```text
alpha_r/gamma_i=2/[3s(s-1)]=alpha_s,                (2.4)
```

division gives

```text
||ell_(b,a)||_(-1,b)^2/q_(b,a)
 =alpha_s ||phi-bar phi||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2/bar phi.    (2.5)
```

Equivalently, if `p^ctx_s=alpha_s phi`, the right side is exactly

```text
||p^ctx_s-E p^ctx_s||_(-1,Pbar_s)^2/E p^ctx_s.      (2.6)
```

Thus the global normalization cancels completely: no factor depending on
`r` is lost in passing to the split branch.  This is the effective-resistance
form in which a recursive proof could be additive rather than multiplying a
Radon--Nikodym loss at every depth.

For `s<=1` the local fibre is a singleton and both sides vanish, so (2.3)
has the natural zero convention rather than a division by `s(s-1)`.

## 3. Why this does not yet prove the target

The contextual local observable `phi` is not a scalar multiple of the
ordinary unary split observable, and no universal shuffle formula has been
proved which converts its position-weighted marked sum to an already bounded
coboundary.  Consequently (2.6) is a full-chain dual norm of a contextual
rate function, not one of the already bounded quotient modes.  Bounding it
by the unknown full spectral gap is circular and loses the powers needed by
the balanced induction.

The smallest surviving constructive proposition is therefore:

> **CONTEXTUAL SPINE COBOUNDARY.**  Construct, for every position-weighted
> contextual rate `p^ctx_s` produced by Theorem 1, an internal `Pbar_s`
> flow routing
> `pi_s(p^ctx_s-Ep^ctx_s)` with energy at most
> `s^C E p^ctx_s`; the sums over all contextual splits must obey the same
> polynomial bound.

Together with (2.3)--(2.6), this proposition proves M54's SPINE-BIAS
H-minus-one BOUND.  The exact audit can refute locality or a proposed
uniform ratio, but its passes cannot prove this proposition.

## 4. Recursive suffix filtration

The constrained-shuffle proof above has a second consequence which is
useful for attacking the remaining coboundary.  It is important here to
retain the positional weights: the false scalar reduction to the ordinary
unary split is not being reinstated.

Fix one contextual function `phi` from Theorem 1, and write `B` for the
size of the suffix subtree which is cut from the augmented unary branch.
For `u in J_s`, let

```text
C(u)=(c_1,...,c_k)
```

be the root composition of its inner tree.  If `c_k>B`, let `v_k` be the
standardized macro of its last root branch.

**Theorem 2 (recursive contextual locality).**  Conditional on a fixed
inner root composition `C`, the following hold universally.

1. If `c_k<B`, then `phi(u)=0`.
2. If `c_k=B`, then `phi(u)` is constant as `u` ranges over the whole
   root-composition fibre `F_C`.
3. If `c_k>B`, then `phi(u)` is a function only of `v_k`.  That function
   is again a position-weighted contextual suffix-cut statistic, now on
   the augmented last branch and with the same suffix size `B`.

### Proof

Expose the unique external root-attachment factor of the augmented unary
branch as a distinguished singleton.  Conditional on `C`, split every
remaining factor into the `k` root-branch subsequences.  The same
Goulden--Yong argument as in Theorem 1 identifies the augmented word with
a constrained shuffle of this singleton and the `k` local words: local
orders are preserved and the `k` root-attachment factors occur in reverse
child order.

The right-spine support theorem says that the rightmost spine enters the
last root branch and never visits an earlier one.  A suffix subtree of size
`B` therefore cannot exist when `c_k<B`, proving part 1.

When `c_k=B`, the cut factor is exactly the distinguished attachment factor
of the last root branch.  For fixed local positions of the external
singleton and all distinguished root factors, the number of constrained
shuffles depends only on the part sizes and those positions.  In each local
orbit the distinguished attachment position is uniform, by the unique-zero
argument (1.3).  Summing over positions and over the local words contributes

```text
product_j |O^+_(v_j)|
```

times a factor depending only on the fixed composition and the inherited
positional weights.  Division by the augmented orbit size cancels every
`|O^+_(v_j)|`; hence the normalized statistic is constant throughout
`F_C`.  This proves part 2.

When `c_k>B`, the marked cut factor lies inside the last branch.  Hold its
local word and marked positions fixed, then sum all words and attachment
positions in the other `k-1` branches.  Exactly as in (1.3)--(1.5), those
orbit factors cancel after normalization.  What remains is a weighted sum
over the last-branch word in which the weights depend only on the fixed
outer context, `C`, and the marked local positions.  This is precisely a
new position-weighted contextual statistic on `v_k`; no other branch macro
remains.  This proves part 3.  QED

Thus recursion follows one strictly smaller last branch; it does not branch
over every child.  Its terminal term is a function of root composition
alone.  The exact falsifier
`recursive_contextual_locality.py` finds no failure of any of the three
claims through `r=7` (272 top groups and 679 deep groups at `r=7`).  These
finite counts are calibration only; the theorem is the constrained-shuffle
argument above.

Theorem 2 narrows the open step but does not by itself bound energy.  A
quotient flow for the terminal composition function, when disintegrated
over actual fine edges, creates target-bias charges of exactly the same
contextual class.  Bounding each disintegration by a fixed factor and then
multiplying down a depth-`Theta(s)` spine would still be exponential.
The sharp remaining form is:

> **ADDITIVE CONTEXTUAL SPINE COBBOUNDARY.**  Lift the root-composition
> flow for the terminal terms in Theorem 2 so that every fine target-bias
> charge is routed recursively down its unique active last branch, with
> total (not per-level) energy at most `s^C E p^ctx_s`.  Equivalently,
> prove CONTEXTUAL SPINE COBBOUNDARY with an additive occupation bound for
> the one-active-branch recursion.

This is strictly smaller than arbitrary ROOT-MEAN LIFT: universal support,
contextual locality, exact normalization cancellation, one-active-branch
closure, and top-fibre constancy are now proved.  What remains is the
additive effective-resistance estimate.
# Exact additive-flow recurrence and its first missing coefficient

Date: 2026-08-11.  This note uses the full nonlazy parking projection
`Pbar_s`, its stationary law `pi_s`, and

```text
alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)].
```

It concerns only the minimal long-cycle sector, not the original identity
bridge chain `K`.

## 1. A contextual demand and its root filtration

Fix one contextual suffix-cut observable supplied by the universal locality
theorem, and normalize it as

```text
f=alpha_s phi >=0,       q=E_(pi_s) f.
```

The fixed suffix size is `B`.  For a root composition
`C=(c_1,...,c_k)`, put `h(C)=E[f|C]` and split the composition space into

```text
Z={C:c_k<B},  T={C:c_k=B},  D={C:c_k>B}.
```

Recursive contextual locality proves:

- `f=0` on every `Z` fibre;
- `f=h(C)` is constant on every `T` fibre;
- on a `D` fibre, `f` depends only on the standardized last-branch
  macro and is another contextual suffix-cut observable.

Define the exact deep-continuation fraction

```text
delta(f)=E[f 1_D]/q.                                 (1.1)
```

## 2. Telescoping of the internal recursive demand

Fix `C in D`, let `t=c_k-1<s` be the number of internal edges in its
last branch, and write the induced lower-rank contextual observable as
`f_t=alpha_t phi_t`.  The constrained-shuffle normalization and the
product restriction give the same coefficient

```text
gamma_(s,t)=t(t-1)/[s(s-1)]=alpha_s/alpha_t,
f=gamma_(s,t) f_t,
E_C=gamma_(s,t) E_(Pbar_t)+other nonnegative coordinates.   (2.1)
```

Suppose a lower-rank flow routes
`pi_t(f_t-Ef_t)` with energy at most `T_t E f_t`.  Scale that flow by
`gamma_(s,t)` and embed it in the last coordinate.  Its demand is exactly
`pi(.|C)(f-h(C))), while its conditional energy is

```text
gamma_(s,t)^2/[gamma_(s,t)] T_t E f_t
 =T_t h(C).                                         (2.2)
```

After multiplying by `rho_s(C)` and summing over `D`, all internal
recursive demands therefore cost at most

```text
delta(f) q max_(t<s) T_t.                           (2.3)
```

There is no Radon--Nikodym loss in (2.3).  Along active sizes
`s=s_0>s_1>...>s_j`, both the demand and capacity coefficients telescope:

```text
product_i gamma_(s_(i-1),s_i)
 =s_j(s_j-1)/[s(s-1)]=alpha_s/alpha_(s_j).          (2.4)
```

## 3. Exact quotient disintegration coefficient

Let `R_s` be the accepted stationary-flow root-composition quotient and
`Q_R(C,C')=rho_s(C)R_s(C,C')`.  Route the mean charge

```text
rho_s(C)(h(C)-q)
```

by a quotient electrical flow `theta`.  Put

```text
a(f)=(1/q) sum_e theta_e^2/Q_R(e)
    =||h-q||_(-1,R_s)^2/q.                          (3.1)
```

For one quotient edge `e=(A,B)`, disintegrate `theta_e` over the actual
fine crossing edges in proportion to stationary flow.  If `A` is the
refined composition and `B` the coarse one, the fixed merge boundary has
constant pointwise rate on `A`.  Thus the refined endpoint is exactly
`pi(.|A)`.  At a coarse state `x`, the endpoint density is

```text
p_e(x)/q_e,   p_e(x)=Pbar_s(x,F_A),
q_e=E_(pi(.|B))p_e,
```

and the residual fine demand is exactly

```text
theta_e pi(x|B)[p_e(x)/q_e-1].                      (3.2)
```

The contextual locality and norm-cancellation theorem turns (3.2) into a
strictly lower-rank contextual demand.  If its normalized flow cost is at
most `T_<s`, scaling its base flow gives energy exactly

```text
T_<s theta_e^2/Q_R(e).                              (3.3)
```

Hence, in the marked network in which residual commodities belonging to
different quotient edges have separate capacity copies, (2.3) and
(3.1)--(3.3) give the exact recurrence

```text
T_s(f) <= a(f)+[delta(f)+a(f)] max_(t<s)T_t.         (3.4)
```

This derivation retains all factors `rho(B)`, `q_e`, `gamma`, and
`alpha`; in particular, (3.3) is neither `T theta_e/q_e` nor
`T theta_e^2/q_e^2`.

## 4. The sufficient scalar absorption inequality

The scalar estimate

```text
a(f)<=1-delta(f)                                    (4.1)
```

would make the recursive coefficient in (3.4) at most one.  If the marked
commodities can also be projected to actual capacities without a
multiplicative collision loss, then

```text
T_s<=1+max_(t<s)T_t<=s.                             (4.2)
```

Thus every individual split coefficient would be at most `s`; summing
over at most `r` one-split refinements would prove M54's H-minus bound
with a fixed polynomial.  M41 Section 11 and M50's balanced induction would
then give an inverse-polynomial gap for the full parking projection.

The exact scalar proposition is:

> **CONTEXTUAL QUOTIENT ABSORPTION.**  For every contextual suffix-cut
> observable produced by constrained-shuffle disintegration,
> ```text
> ||E[f|root composition]-Ef||_(-1,R_s)^2
>   <= E[f 1_{last root branch size = B}].
> ```
> The right side equals `q(1-delta(f))` because the observable vanishes
> when the last branch is smaller than `B`.

This has not been proved.  Applying only the accepted quotient gap gives
`a(f)<=3e Var(h)/q`, which does not compare sharply enough with the
terminal mass and would multiply a constant once per spine depth.

## 5. The separate capacity-collision obligation

Even (4.1) is not alone sufficient.  Equations (3.3)--(3.4) add the
energies of edge-labelled residual commodities.  In the actual unmarked
chain, recursively routed commodities can share an internal edge.  The
inequality

```text
(sum_j F_j(e))^2/Q(e) <= sum_j F_j(e)^2/Q(e)
```

is false without cancellation or disjointness.  A crude Cauchy bound by
the number of contexts introduces a factor as large as `s` at every
depth and destroys (4.2).

The exact remaining flow proposition is therefore:

> **MARKED ADDITIVE SOURCE RECOVERY.**  Choose the quotient flows and their
> recursively disintegrated contextual flows so that each actual fine edge
> can recover its active-depth/root-boundary history with total squared
> load bounded by the right side of (3.4), up to one universal polynomial
> added over all depths, not multiplied at every depth.

Root-composition martingale differences at different active depths use
rotations at different vertices, so a depth mark is a plausible recovery
key.  No universal injection or fractional collision bound has yet been
proved.

## 6. Exact bounded falsification

`contextual_macro_energy.py` computes `a(f)`, `delta(f)`, and their
sum for every ambient split context through `r=7`.  There is no quotient
nullspace failure.  The largest observed values of
`delta(f)+a(f)` are

```text
ambient r       3        4        5        6        7
maximum       .5278    .6667    .7569    .8178    .8634
```

(the last displayed decimal is rounded upward; the stored value is about
`.8633184`).  The largest observed ratio
`a(f)/(1-delta(f))` is about `.382884`.  Thus (4.1) survives this
bounded falsifier with slack.  These floating electrical solves are finite
diagnostics only; they prove neither (4.1) nor the source-recovery claim.

The smallest open implication is CONTEXTUAL QUOTIENT ABSORPTION.  After it,
MARKED ADDITIVE SOURCE RECOVERY is still required before (4.2) is a proof
for the actual chain.

