# Resolution Ledger: Local Heat-Bath Polynomial Mixing

STATUS: ACTIVE
STRONGEST RESULT: Qualitative irreducibility of K, J, and every nonempty arbitrary-endpoint aligned-H4 bridge is proved. The m=4 gap is at least 1/4; K dominates B by 1/12 and J by 1/(3 binom(N,2)^2). Independently audited bridge reductions show that one base length R_N=O(N log N) controls every longer Hamiltonian with loss at most 4(R_N-1); pair lengths three and four have independently accepted gaps M^-16 and 2/(3M^20). An exact leave-one-coordinate recursion reduces the complete-pair bridge gap to a normal coordinate-correlation Gram operator with O(N^4) active range, and pointwise smoothing bounds its retention norm by 5/(4l) above C_mix N log(N+1). Microfiber coordinate modes have exact retention 1/l. In the minimal long-cycle sector every fixed parking-multiset restriction has an inverse-polynomial gap. An independently audited Lorentzian clone down-up chain on the parking-multiset projection has gap at least 1/r; a canonical comparison reduces it to adjacent-value ideal moves with gap at least r^-7. Exact parking leaf rotations have rates 2m_i/[3r(r-1)] and 2/[3r(r-1)]. The full parking projection has an independently accepted root-degree projection gap at least 4(r+1)/[3r^2(r-1)], and its exact root-composition quotient has frozen gap at least 2/[9e r(r-1)] with product-form restrictions. The exact stationary-flow projection of uniform Cayley-tree basis exchange has gap at least 1/r and the correct parking law; comparison to the actual projection is open. A fresh referee accepts a weighted deletion-flow proof that the conditioned-Poisson Metropolis leaf-replanting chain has gap at least 1/[16(r+1)^8]. The audited macro projection dominates square down-up S by 1/[24(m-2)]; dense support partitions, color projections, all one-gate modes, and square-deletion action rates have inverse-polynomial bounds. Full macro restrictions are polynomially controlled by their connected-Hurwitz-coordinate gaps through an independently accepted shuttle flow. On the refutation side, for N>=10^12 and m=4N^3+4 every literal disconnected-macro neighborhood through radius floor(m/10^4) has conductance at least N^-25; the smaller m/10^8 theorem has independently passed a fresh referee. At minimal length, a freshly accepted theorem gives conductance at least 1/(24N^7) for both global placements of every arbitrary subset of labeled join trees; therefore all join-tree-saturated cuts are ruled out as Terminal-B witnesses.
  Freshly accepted extension: every nonempty subset `A` of the entire minimal connected macro satisfies `Q_K(A,A^c)/pi(A)>=1/(24N^13)`, and both macro-closed lifts follow by complement symmetry.  A frozen exterior-closure theorem now gives exact full-boundary identities, inverse-polynomial conductance for every fixed shell radius, and polynomial-diameter saturation of the entire exterior; only growing intermediate radii remain open.  In the accepted minimal-long-cycle analysis, the M67 additive mode has Rayleigh quotient `O(l^-3/2)` for the complete-pair, aligned-adjacent, and fixed-endpoint local chains, while every nonzero cyclic-frequency sector in its invariant closure has an explicit inverse-polynomial gap.  The sole unresolved sector of that endpoint family is the cyclically invariant orbit-incidence quotient.
SMALLEST OPEN IMPLICATION: Establish BASE-SCALE FIXED-ENDPOINT GAP uniformly through pair length O(N log N). The definitive, independently accepted M67 theorem refutes the hoped-for O(1/l) coordinate-correlation rate: minimal long-cycle endpoints have liminf sqrt(l) mu_l at least 1.50977. M70/M72 then show that this mode is only polynomially slow and that every nonzero cyclic-frequency sector of its exceptional closure is polynomially controlled; the exact residual is CYCLIC-ORBIT INCIDENCE GAP in the invariant sector. Within the parking-flow route, CONTEXTUAL QUOTIENT ABSORPTION and even its proposed 1+O(1/s) relaxation are refuted for the marked scalar recurrence. Exact marked-context inheritance retains positional/history weights and cannot be replaced by the ordinary `(k,0)` family. The surviving obligations are CYCLIC-ORBIT INCIDENCE GAP, a polynomial ROOT-MEAN LIFT via marked weighted Green contraction or another actual parking-flow argument, and INTERMEDIATE EXTERIOR-LAYER EXPANSION. The restricted leaf-rotation comparison has an independently checked reversible-pebbling obstruction and is no longer viable alone. A base bridge theorem would still imply Terminal A through the audited reductions; alternatively Terminal B requires an explicit infinite superpolynomial full-K obstruction. Nonirreducibility is ruled out.
ACTIVE ASSIGNMENTS: Cycle 16: M71 attacks a polynomial marked root-mean flow with actual-edge recovery; M73 attacks the cyclic-orbit incidence gap by an equivariant Cayley-tree/basis-exchange comparison or a literal obstruction; M75 attacks the accepted M68/M74 one-radius partial-macro marked-cover/coarea frontier.
