The fresh M75 referee is now running against the frozen hashes. Separately, M73 found that two steps already have full support, but pointwise relative minorization is too strong; the stable object is instead the pairwise Dobrushin coefficient, empirically \(O(\ell^{-2})\). Its extremal pair is geometrically explicit—balanced thirds versus a near-balanced double-transposition—so the analytic proof target is now much narrower.
