codex
The counterexample is now infinite and clean: its degree-two reset edges alone contribute
\[
q_s^3\sum_{A=1}^{s-1}\left(\frac{A}{A+1}\right)^2
= q_s^3\bigl(s-2H_s+H_s^{(2)}\bigr),
\]
so the inverse-\(q\) potential grows linearly and even the \(1+C/P\) relaxation fails. Importantly, this is a failure of that weighting, not yet of renewal itself: on the same family I independently find the *unweighted* reset row mass tending only to about \(0.27\). The next plausible invariant is therefore direct substochastic reset occupation, with strict rank descent supplying the polynomial time horizon.
