cross edge is a join and the second is a cut, and therefore

```text
T_J(target)=J_U union J_V union {s}.
```

Because `A` is contained in one fixed join-tree fibre, at most one choice of
`s` can enter `A`; all constants are unchanged.

The theorem also proves an exact sufficient cover lemma: `L` fixed
state-independent Hurwitz words of length at most `D` that cover a partial
macrofibre by connected deletable-square states give boundary at least
`|S|/[6(m-2)M^2LD]`, with explicit source recovery.  Several tempting covers
are rigorously refuted: direct two-position deletion, a four-null strand
variant, colors-only braid handles, and a full-arc lift with infinite pure-
braid fibres.  Direct algebraic insertion certificates have polynomial upper
Radon--Nikodym density but vanish on explicit states.

