### L-0206 - Randomized partial-macro coarea is proved and freshly accepted

M75 freezes report SHA-256
`e699e8b54684488ae34a8df87edea5f9a88002939e34d9facc55c549b741ed39`
and manifest SHA-256
`17bb22b3c041ec1917f206d0a3cf9a8fba2f049fd5a6b61da2eb004699a6b89b`.
Its main theorem replaces a finite deterministic cover by a
state-independent probability law on bijective Hurwitz words.  If every
source reaches a marked set at a prefix with probability at least `eta`, the
mean word length is at most `D`, and every charged actual chain edge has
capacity at least `p`, then every partial subset `S` satisfies

```text
sum_(x in S) K(x,(Gamma\S) union T) >= p eta |S|/(D+1).
```

For endpoint-only hits the denominator improves to `max(D,1)`.  A word,
time, and charged edge recover the original source by the inverse prefix, so
the support cardinality of the word law does not enter the congestion.  The
argument includes countable word laws and positive mass on the empty word.

Once a two-component exterior word has a connected identity-preserving
two-deletion certificate, the M60 null-push algebra gives a literal
polynomial path to an adjacent square: writing `w=P x U y S` and
`z=P U S`, cancellation forces `x=U y U^-1`; a right Hurwitz bubble produces
`P U y y S`.  The path has length at most `m-1`, preserves the weighted
support macro, and has polynomial source recovery.  Thus the remaining
two-component question is exactly a worst-source mark-hitting estimate, not
a factorial-word-family congestion problem.

M75 also gives an exact route refutation.  The displayed `N=6,m=10` exterior
word has two identity-preserving deletion pairs, both disconnected; none of
its eighteen signed adjacent Hurwitz neighbours has a connected certificate,
while exactly 104 signed two-step paths do.  Hence an identity-or-one-move
certificate cover is false.  Uniform simple positive permutation braids have
mean length `m(m-1)/4` and a doubly regular incidence multigraph, but this
proves only the average marked hit.  Exact `S_3,m=6` row counts range from
`608` to `720`, so the needed polynomial worst-row lower bound remains open.
For three or more components, a separate additive merger-occupation theorem
is still required.

M77 independently accepts M75 with no objection or correction.  It checks
the randomized first-crossing normalization, the zero-length endpoint case,
literal interleaved null pushing, all heat-bath probabilities, the complete
radius-two witness enumeration, and the distinction between double
regularity and a row minimum.  Its report is
`cycle-16/mission-M77-m75-fresh-referee/report.md`, SHA-256
`ad09b58a061e8b65382a3fff316e846ef291b06de761fbad79711cf9b645fd44`;
manifest SHA-256
`a46bf8986839a0e912792266e63b7408dec75bc54ceac2c0943ee81aaae0c0b1`.

Verdict: RANDOMIZED COAREA IMPLICATION AND POST-CERTIFICATE RECOVERY PROVED
AND FRESHLY ACCEPTED; RADIUS-ONE COVER REFUTED; NONTERMINAL.

