### L-0044 - Dense arbitrary-cut partition expansion and exact allocation chain

Fresh M03 audit accepts every frozen M02 macro weight, transition formula,
`D_N`, comparison constant, and `S`/aligned-`B` connectivity claim.  Its
independent exact Fraction harness reproduces all required small cases,
including rows, detailed balance, common-core conductances, and comparison
inequalities.

More substantially, for `m-2>=4M log(2N)`, M03 proves that the projection
`Pi` of `S` onto exact labeled support partitions satisfies

    Phi(Pi) >= 3/(16M^2),
    gap(Pi) >= 9/(512M^4).

This controls every subset of the partition state space.  The proof uses the
target-wise dense child-mass estimate `sum_{C:F(C)=P}nu(C)<=4nu(P)/N^4`, a
root of mass at least `3/4`, and an actual parent edge of probability at least
`1/(4M^2)`.  Decomposing an arbitrary smaller-side set into rooted-tree
components charges distinct top boundary edges, so no threshold rearrangement
or canonical hub is hidden.

For a fixed partition with nontrivial block sizes `v_i`, surplus allocation
`g`, `E_i=binom(v_i,2)`, and
`rho_v(g)=a_v(g-1)/a_v(g)`, the standard rejected-exit restriction is exactly

    S_P(g,g-e_i+e_j)
      = E_i E_j rho_{v_i}(g_i)/[M m(m-1)].

It has the product stationary law `prod_i a_{v_i}(g_i)` and dominates the
same-law uniform-destination zero-range chain by `q/[M m(m-1)]`.  The cited
Boudou--Caputo--Dai Pra--Posta theorem would give its gap from a uniform lower
increment of `rho`.  M12's theorem already supplies `rho_v(g)>=12/v^3`, so
the action rate is polynomial; it does not control the increment.  The
ultra-log-concavity shortcut is exactly false at `v=4,g=1`, with margin
`-89/1066`, while ordinary increments remain positive only in finite tested
cases.

JSTV bookkeeping is exact and yields, conditionally on the minimum allocation
gap `lambda_alloc`,

    gap(S) >= 9 lambda_alloc/(2048M^4),
    gap(barK) >= 9 lambda_alloc/[49152(m-2)M^4].

