### L-0049 - Dispatch two-overlapping-block parity-bridge lane

M11 was recycled into M10 to leave scalar local-mode analysis.  In the exact
grouped parity bridge with increment law `Q=P_transposition^2`, it must compare
continuous-time single-site heat baths with two large overlapping interval
heat baths.  The target is a geometric-scale recursion whose two-block angle
has a universal gap once the overlap exceeds the relative-mixing scale, with
no factor of the path length lost at every scale.  Exact `Q^ell` bridge
kernels, endpoint pins, and microfactor weights must remain.

The lane must either prove this recursion and isolate a polynomial base-scale
proposition, or construct a precise endpoint-conditioned maximal-correlation
obstruction.  Scalar Dobrushin and two-type one-step coupling may not be
reused.  A `B` gap proves the target through `K>=B/12`; a slow `B` mode alone
does not refute `K`.

