# M76 final report: canonical reset renewal and inverse-split-mass frontier

Date: 2026-08-12. Base commit:
`502a6f031c6d5a4bc0064ee5b370a4fa3914f993`.

## 1. Exact claim, conventions, status, and scope

Permutations compose as `(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`; factors multiply left-to-right.
This mission concerns only the full **nonlazy stationary-flow parking-degree
projection** `Pbar_r` in the minimal factorization sector of
`(0 1 ... r)`. It is not a theorem for the original identity-bridge chain
`K`.

For local rank `s`, write

```text
G_s=R_s/alpha_s,                 alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)],
rho_s(C)=w_(s+1)^(-1)[1/k!] product_i w_(c_i),
w_a=a^(a-1)/a!,
q_x=w_(s+1-B)w_B/w_(s+1),       x=(s,K,R,B).
```

Let `D` be M65's exact marked deep kernel, `J=J_can` the residual kernel
from M50's first-boundary canonical root flow, and `a=a_can` its normalized
base energy. Pure-deep elimination gives

```text
b=(I-D)^(-1)a,              K_reset=(I-D)^(-1)J.    (1.1)
```

This report proves strict acyclicity, exact reset reachability, an infinite
obstruction to every fixed-power one-step potential in the tested families,
and an exact one-dimensional seed-kernel formula. It reduces polynomial
occupation to one explicit inverse-split-mass inequality for `K_reset`.
That inequality remains **unresolved**. Consequently no polynomial energy
comparison for actual `Pbar_r`, no ROOT-MEAN LIFT, and no result for `K` is
claimed here.

## 2. Proved phase geometry and exact reachability

Put

```text
u=K-R,                    P(x)=s+u.
```

A deep child arising from a `k`-part root composition with last part `t`
and attachment rank `j>=1` is

```text
y=(t-1,K+k,R+j,B).
```

If `n=s-t` is the prefix mass, its `k-1` positive parts give `n>=k-1`,
and therefore

```text
P(x)-P(y)=s-t+1-k+j=n-k+j+1>=j>=1.                 (2.1)
```

A used canonical edge has refined endpoint
`(A,c_2,...,c_k)` and merges its first two parts. Its residual child is

```text
y=(A+c_2-1,k-1,k-2,c_2),
P(y)=A+c_2<=s<P(x).                                 (2.2)
```

Thus `D+J` is a finite DAG under the strictly descending integer `P`; all
resolvents in (1.1) are finite algebraic sums, not analytic limits.

Every reset child has `K-R=1`. Starting at the seed `(K,R)=(1,0)`, one
deep step with `k=K'-1,j=R'` reaches every `K'>R'>=1`. Conversely `j>=1`
precludes every formal mark `R=0,K>1`. Hence the exact reachable closure is

```text
{(1,0)} union {(K,R):K>R>=1}.                       (2.3)
```

This matters in potential scans: the worst formal inverse-weight rows with
`R=0,K>1` are not generated by canonical resets.

## 3. Fixed-power one-step certificates are universally false

Fix any finite exponent `d>=0` and take the right-heavy family

```text
x_s=(s,K_s,K_s-1,s-1),          K_s=s^2.
```

The unary root composition supplies a deep child with coefficient exactly
`K_s/(K_s+1)`, child `P=s`, child `u=1`, and child suffix excess plus one
`ell=1`. The canonical degree-two edge `(s-1,1)->(s)` has source basin
`Z={last part=1}` and reset child `(s-1,1,0,1)`. On `Z`, the parent
contextual mean is zero. Since the edge capacity equals `q_x`, its reset
coefficient is exactly

```text
p_s^2,               p_s=rho_s(last part=1).
```

The single composition `(s-1,1)` gives

```text
p_s>=w_(s-1)/(2w_(s+1))->e^(-2)/2.                 (3.1)
```

Both displayed children have `P=s`. Therefore the one-step ratio for
`V=P^d u` has lower limit

```text
1+e^(-4)/4>1.                                       (3.2)
```

For `V=P^d u[1+log ell]`, the same two terms give the lower bound

```text
(s/(s+1))^d [K_s/(K_s+1)+p_s^2(1+log(s-1))]
              /(1+log 2),                          (3.3)
```

which diverges. Thus **every fixed exponent** in both proposed one-step
families is refuted. This is not an occupation counterexample: the reset
lands at `B=1`, and the subsequent deep excursion is exactly the
cancellation discarded by a one-step maximum.

## 4. Exact reset renewal and the inverse-split-mass reduction

The exact finite reset row sums `K_reset 1` over every right-heavy seed
through `s=14`, with `K=1,...,16,64,128,256,1024,4096`, have maxima

```text
s       3      4      5      6      7      8      9     10
max   .160   .279   .356   .444   .497   .538   .578   .609

s      11     12     13     14
max   .633   .656   .675   .691.
```

Every maximum occurs at `(K,R)=(1,0)`. These values are exact finite-DAG
floating evaluations and prove no asymptotic inequality.

The structurally natural potential is the reciprocal stationary split
mass

```text
h(x)=1/q_x=w_(s+1)/[w_(s+1-B)w_B].                 (4.1)
```

For a deep child, `q_y=w_(t-B)w_B/w_t`; for a canonical reset child in
(2.2), `q_y=w_Aw_(c_2)/w_(A+c_2)`. Thus the factors in (4.1) cancel the
same split weights already present in `D` and `J`.

The decisive remaining statement is

```text
sum_y K_reset(x,y) h(y) <= h(x)                     (4.2)
```

for every right-heavy `x`. The accepted M50 split estimate gives

```text
1<=h(x)<=(3/4)(s+1)^(3/2).                          (4.3)
```

Equation (4.2) is sufficient for polynomial occupation. Indeed `D` is
substochastic and strictly lowers `P`, while M71 proved

```text
a(x)<=e(1+log s)min(s,K-R)<=eP(1+log P).
```

Consequently every pure-deep base excursion obeys
`b(x)<=eP^2(1+log P)`. Since `J` lands right-heavy, (4.2) iterates:
if `mu_n=delta_x K_reset^n`, then `mu_n h<=h(x)` and hence
`mu_n 1<=h(x)`. Strict `P` descent makes `mu_n=0` for `n>=P(x)`. Therefore
the full separated marked base occupation is at most

```text
sum_(n<P) mu_n b
 <=e P^3(1+log P)h(x)
 <=(3e/4)P^(9/2)(1+log P).                          (4.4)
```

M71's one-shot `O(r^9)` actual-edge label Cauchy bound would then make the
unmarking loss polynomial as well.

Finite evidence isolates why (4.2), rather than a raw inequality, is the
right target. Through `s=14`, `K=1,...,16,64,256,4096`, the largest
eliminated inverse-`q` ratio is `.761049`, at
`(s,K,R,B)=(14,4096,4095,1)`. Including `b` gives `.974109`. In contrast,
the raw `(D+J)h/h` ratio is already `1.08505` there, and the raw ratio
including `a` is `1.14727`. Pure-deep elimination is essential.

## 5. Proved one-dimensional seed-kernel identity

For a seed `(K,R)=(1,0)`, define the Cayley coefficients

```text
A_a=[z^a](e^T-1)/T
   =sum_(p-part compositions of a) product w/(p+1)!,

C_a=[z^a]int_0^1 u e^(uT)du
   =[z^a]((T-1)e^T+1)/T^2
   =sum_(p-part compositions of a)(p+1)product w/(p+2)!.
```

For the degree-two canonical reset with child suffix `t`, basin summation
gives

```text
p_t=P(last=t)=w_t A_(s-t)/w_(s+1),
q_B=w_(s+1-B)w_B/w_(s+1),

M_B(t)=0,                                           t<B,
       =w_B A_(s-B)/w_(s+1),                       t=B,
       =w_(t-B)w_B C_(s-t)/w_(s+1),               t>B.
```

The exact residual entry is

```text
J_s(B,t)=[M_B(t)-q_Bp_t]^2
          /{[w_(s-t)w_t/w_(s+1)]q_B}.              (5.1)
```

Proof: the canonical basin consists of all ordered refinements of its
merged first part. Summing `rho(H-q_B)` over those refinements gives
`M_B(t)-q_Bp_t`; the normalized edge capacity is the displayed split
flow. Expanding by the number of prefix parts produces `A` and `C`.

The child rank is `s-1`; (5.1) is not a same-rank loop. It agrees with
every direct composition entry through `s=10` within `2e-12`. The scaled
implementation uses `v_a=e^{-a}w_a`: `p_t,M_B,Q_G` each acquire exactly
one factor `e^{-1}`, while `q_B` is invariant. A literal scaled/unscaled
assertion at `s=12` has maximum relative coefficient error `5.68e-16` and
kernel error `8.63e-14`.

## 6. Probability, normalization, runtime, and congestion accounting

- Every canonical coefficient is `theta_e^2/[Q_G(e)q_x]`, where
  `theta_e=sum_(C in basin)rho_s(C)(H(C)-q_x)` and the normalized refined
  edge capacity is `Q_G(e)=rho_s(C)k`.
- A deep coefficient is stationary group mass times the child split mean
  and M65's negative-hypergeometric attachment weight, divided by `q_x`.
  Its row sum is the exact deep fraction `delta<=1`.
- The actual scan factor is always `alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)]`; M56's
  `alpha/gamma` norm cancellation is the accepted conversion between the
  displayed `G_s` recurrence and embedded `Pbar_s` energy.
- M50's canonical basin occurrence bound is at most `e`; M71's base bound
  uses the harmonic first-merge path factor `1+log s`.
- The reset-renewal run has `2^(s-1)` root compositions and took `21.22`
  seconds through `s=14`; its recorded deep-mass identity error is zero at
  floating precision. The inverse-`q` audit took `19.10` seconds. The
  grouped seed formula reached `s=125` in `.19` seconds.
- Python was `3.12.3`, NumPy `1.26.4`, and SciPy `1.11.4`; all runs are
  deterministic and record seed `null`.
- M71 proved at most `O(r^9)` recoverable
  `(embedding,s,K,R,B,nearest reset)` labels per actual edge and applies
  Cauchy once after aggregation. That result is conditional here on first
  proving polynomial marked occupation.
- Two obsolete broad discovery scans were terminated before freeze after
  about 52 and 15 minutes; neither produced nor supports a reported claim.

## 7. Dependencies and claim ledger

- **Proved/frozen M50/M41:** root-composition law and exact merge/split
  capacities; first-boundary canonical basin recovery; split lower bound;
  balanced reduction from ROOT-MEAN LIFT.
- **Proved/frozen M56:** contextual branch locality, exact `H^{-1}` norm
  cancellation, and marked additive recurrence.
- **Proved/frozen/refereed M65/M69:** closed contextual mean,
  negative-hypergeometric inheritance, and refutation of scalar contextual
  absorption.
- **Proved M71:** right-heavy canonical reset, canonical base bound, exact
  deep suffix contraction, and one-shot polynomial actual-edge label
  multiplicity.
- **Proved here:** strict `P` descent; reachable mark closure; the infinite
  fixed-power one-step obstructions (3.2)--(3.3); seed identity (5.1); and
  the conditional polynomial implication (4.2) `=>` (4.4).
- **Exact finite falsifiers only:** renewal row sums, inverse-`q` ratios,
  grouped potentials, and seed-kernel scans.
- **Unresolved:** (4.2), polynomial marked occupation, actual unmarked
  ROOT-MEAN LIFT, the auxiliary `Pbar` gap, and every claim for `K`.

## 8. First unproved lemma and strongest self-attack

> **DEEP-ELIMINATED INVERSE-SPLIT-MASS SUPERSOLUTION.** For every
> `s>=2`, `K>=1`, `1<=B<=s`, and right-heavy seed
> `x=(s,K,K-1,B)`, let `D,J_can` have the exact normalizations in Field 1.
> Then
> ```text
> sum_y [(I-D)^(-1)J_can](x,y)/q_y <=1/q_x.          (8.1)
> ```

A relaxed factor `1+C/P(x)` also suffices, because `P` decreases at every
reset and its product is polynomial.

No martingale proof is being smuggled into (8.1). Canonical basin currents
are not orthogonal Doob increments: the raw inverse-`q` inequality fails,
one-step `a+delta` exceeds one from the bounded rank-10 scan onward, and the
eliminated reset mass is not bounded by `Var(H)/q` in the tested seeds.
The finite `.761` margin can shrink or reverse after `s=14`; it is evidence
for selecting (8.1), not evidence that (8.1) is true.

Conversely, the one-step counterfamily in Field 3 does not refute (8.1).
Its reset child changes the suffix phase from `B=s-1` to `B=1`, precisely
where the eliminated inverse-`q` weighting gains room. An actual obstruction
must evaluate the full pure-deep excursion or exhibit an infinite family
violating (8.1), not reuse the raw two-child ratio.

## 9. Artifacts, reproduction, exact verdict, and handoff

Primary proof artifacts are `plan.md`, `checkpoint.md`, and this report.
Reproducible diagnostics are:

```text
python3 -B reset_renewal_probe.py --s-max 14 --K-max 16 \
  --exponents 1 2 3 4 --excess-powers 0 1 \
  --output reset_renewal_s14_k16.json

python3 -B inverse_q_renewal_probe.py --s-max 14 --K-max 16 \
  --K-slices 64 256 4096 --output inverse_q_renewal_s14.json

python3 -B seed_kernel_probe.py --s-values 10 20 40 80 125 \
  --output seed_kernel_s125.json
```

The remaining potential and grouped-DP files document rejected discovery
routes; none is a proof dependency.

**Exact verdict: INCONCLUSIVE — PROMOTE THE REDUCTION, NOT THE THEOREM.**
M76 neither proves universal canonical reset occupation nor finds an
infinite obstruction surviving deep elimination. It replaces the broad
occupation problem by the standalone scalar operator inequality (8.1),
with exact polynomial closure if that inequality holds.

Manuscript-ready handoff: *For the canonical first-boundary flow, the marked
history operator is nilpotent under `P=s+K-R`. Every fixed-power one-step
Lyapunov certificate can fail, but after eliminating pure-deep excursions
the only missing estimate is inverse stationary split-mass
superharmonicity (8.1). This estimate would give `O(P^(9/2)log P)` separated
marked occupation and, with the previously proved one-shot `O(r^9)` label
unmarking, a polynomial actual-edge comparison for auxiliary `Pbar`.*
# Canonical marked-flow reduction and exact deep contraction

Date: 2026-08-12.  This note concerns only the full nonlazy
minimal-long-cycle parking projection `Pbar_s`.  It is not a theorem about
the identity bridge chain `K`.

## 1. Normalization and status

Permutations compose as `(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`, and factor tuples multiply
left-to-right.  Write

```text
alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)],              G_s=R_s/alpha_s,
rho_s(C)=w_(s+1)^(-1) [1/k!] product_i w_(c_i),
w_a=a^(a-1)/a!,                   C=(c_1,...,c_k).
```

For a contextual mark `x=(s,K,R,B)`, let `H_x` be M65's root-composition
conditional mean and

```text
q_x=E_rho H_x=w_(s+1-B)w_B/w_(s+1).
```

Sections 2--6 below are universal proved statements.  Section 7 is a
proved audit explaining why they do not yet give an actual-edge flow.
The surviving proposition is isolated in Section 9.

## 2. Every canonical quotient residual resets to a right-heavy mark

Route a root-composition charge to the one-part hub by repeatedly merging
the first two parts.  A used quotient edge has refined endpoint

```text
e: (A,c_2,...,c_k) -> (A+c_2,c_3,...,c_k),          k>=2.       (2.1)
```

In M56's residual formula, the boundary position `p` is the number of
displayed boundaries strictly to the left of the merged boundary.  Thus
the first-boundary route has `p=0`.  Substitution in M71 equation (H.1)
gives the child

```text
y_e=(A+c_2-1, k-1, k-2, c_2).                      (2.2)
```

In particular, every quotient child is right-heavy:

```text
K_y-R_y=1.                                         (2.3)
```

This is an exact accounting statement.  It does not say that later deep
inheritance remains right-heavy; a deep child is
`(t-1,K+k,R+j,B)` and can have `K-R+k-j>1`.

## 3. Canonical quotient energy

Put `g=H_x-q_x`.  For (2.1), let `B_e` be the M50 source basin: all
compositions obtained by arbitrarily refining `A`, with the displayed
suffix `(c_2,...,c_k)` fixed.  The canonical current is

```text
theta_x(e)=sum_(C in B_e) rho_s(C)g(C).             (3.1)
```

This has the correct divergence `rho_s g`, because the first-merge edges
form a tree oriented to the one-part hub.  M50 gives

```text
rho_s(B_e)<=e rho_s((A,c_2,...,c_k)),
Q_G(e)=rho_s((A,c_2,...,c_k)) k.                    (3.2)
```

Cauchy--Schwarz and (3.2) imply

```text
theta_x(e)^2/Q_G(e)
 <=(e/k) sum_(C in B_e)rho_s(C)g(C)^2.              (3.3)
```

A source composition with `ell` parts belongs to exactly the basins of
the edges on its deterministic merge path, whose refined part counts are
`ell,ell-1,...,2`.  Summing (3.3) therefore proves

```text
E_can(g):=sum_e theta_x(e)^2/Q_G(e)
 <=e H_s^(harm) Var_rho(H_x)
 <=e(1+log s) Var_rho(H_x).                         (3.4)
```

Here `H_s^(harm)=sum_(j=1)^s 1/j`; it is unrelated to the contextual
mean `H_x`.  All capacities in (3.2)--(3.4) are for `G_s`; returning to `R_s` multiplies
the energy by `alpha_s^(-1)`, exactly as in M56.

There is also a uniform pointwise bound on the closed M65 mean.  First,

```text
w_a w_b/w_(a+b)<=1.                                 (3.5)
```

If `a,b>=2`, the left side is

```text
binom(a+b,a)(a/(a+b))^a(b/(a+b))^b (a+b)/(ab)<=1;
```

the binomial-probability factor is at most one and `ab>=a+b`.  If one
part is one, (3.5) reduces to `((n-1)/n)^(n-2)<=1`.

For the terminal line put `u=K-R`.  The numerator in

```text
T_(K,R)(k)
 =K binom(k+u-2,u-1)/binom(k+K-1,K-1)              (3.6)
```

increases with `u`, so setting `u=K` gives `T<=k`.  For fixed `(u,k)`,
`K/binom(k+K-1,K-1)` is nonincreasing in `K>=u`; setting `K=u` instead
gives `T<=u`.  The deep line is at most one by (3.5) and `D<=1`.
Since `k,u>=1`, this proves

```text
0<=H_x(C)<=min(s,K-R).                              (3.7)
```

For a nonnegative random variable `H<=M`,
`Var(H)<=E H^2<=M E H`.  Combining this with (3.4)--(3.7) yields the
normalized canonical base estimate

```text
a_can(x):=E_can(H_x-q_x)/q_x
 <=e(1+log s) min(s,K-R).                           (3.8)
```

By (2.3), every freshly reset quotient child satisfies the sharper bound

```text
a_can(y_e)<=e(1+log rank(y_e)).                     (3.9)
```

Equation (3.9), rather than an arbitrary-context maximum, is the usable
gain from the canonical route.

## 4. Exact stationary deep-descendant kernel

Put

```text
S=s+1-B,                         L=s-B=S-1.
```

There is no deep continuation when `S=1`.  Suppose `S>=2`, write
`n=s-t` for the total prefix size before the last part, and define

```text
A_n=sum_(p>=0) 1/(p+1)!
       sum_(a_1+...+a_p=n) product_i w_(a_i).        (4.1)
```

The empty prefix contributes `A_0=1`.  After stationary mass, the M65
deep split ratio, and `q_x` are cancelled, the total deep child measure is
bounded by the probability law

```text
P_S(n)=A_n w_(S-n-1)/w_S,          0<=n<=S-2.       (4.2)
```

The only discarded factor is `D_(K,R)(p+1)<=1`; summing the marked
negative-hypergeometric weights gives exactly that `D`.

To normalize (4.2), let

```text
T(z)=sum_(a>=1)w_a z^a=z exp(T(z)),
A(z)=sum_(n>=0)A_n z^n
    =(exp(T(z))-1)/T(z)=1/z-1/T(z).                 (4.3)
```

Then

```text
A(z)T(z)=T(z)/z-1,
```

and the coefficient of `z^(S-1)` is `w_S`, proving normalization.

The first moment is also exact.  From (4.3) and
`zT'(z)/T(z)=1/(1-T(z))`,

```text
sum_n n A_n w_(S-n-1)
 =[z^(S-1)] zA'(z)T(z)
 =[z^(S-1)] {-T(z)/z+1/(1-T(z))}.
```

Lagrange inversion gives

```text
[z^N]1/(1-T(z))=N^(N-1)/(N-1)!,
```

so

```text
E_(P_S)n=(S-1)^(S-1)/S^(S-2)-1.                   (4.4)
```

For `S>=8`, the standard inequality
`(1-1/S)^(S-1)>=e^(-1)` gives

```text
E n >=(S-1)/e-1 >=(S-2)/4.
```

Direct substitution in (4.4) verifies the same inequality for
`2<=S<=7`.  Thus universally

```text
E_(P_S)n >=(S-2)/4.                                (4.5)
```

This strengthens M65's asymptotic descendant calculation to an exact
finite-rank moment bound.

## 5. Fixed-factor suffix-excess contraction

For a deep child, the new suffix excess is

```text
L_y=(t-1)-B=S-n-2=L-1-n.                           (5.1)
```

Let `Wdeep(x,y)` denote the exact coefficient (H.4) in the separated
marked DAG, including the sum over `j`.  Equations (4.2), (4.5), and
`D<=1` prove

```text
sum_y Wdeep(x,y)L_y <=(3/4)(L-1)_+,                  (5.2)
sum_y Wdeep(x,y)(L_y+1) <=(3/4)(L+1).              (5.3)
```

For (5.3), use that the total deep weight is at most one:
the left side is at most
`1+(3/4)(L-1)=(3/4)L+1/4<=(3/4)(L+1)`.
When `L=0` there is no deep child; when `L=1`, every deep child has
`L_y=0`, and the same inequality holds.

Consequently, along a segment containing only deep inheritance, the
expected occupation of `L+1` is at most

```text
sum_(d>=0) (3/4)^d(L+1)=4(L+1).                    (5.4)
```

This is a genuine weighted/non-max contraction.  It handles every
stationary prefix composition and every collision of `j`-marks within the
same deep transition; it does not yet handle a new quotient reset.

## 6. Harmonic positional marks

Let `J` have M65's full negative-hypergeometric law on `0<=J<=k`.
Each of the `k` inner attachments lies before `O_(R+1)` with probability
`(R+1)/(K+1)`, hence

```text
E J=k(R+1)/(K+1).                                  (6.1)
```

For the child `(K+k,R+J)`, (6.1) gives the exact harmonic identities

```text
E [(R+J+1)/(K+k+1)] =(R+1)/(K+1),
E [(K-R+k-J)/(K+k+1)] =(K-R)/(K+1).                (6.2)
```

The actual deep recursion deletes the nonnegative `J=0` term.  Therefore
both fractions in (6.2) are superharmonic for the substochastic marked
deep kernel.  This prevents an exponential count of positional histories
at the level of their total weighted mass.  It does not bound the squared
load created by different quotient-reset origins on one actual edge.

## 7. What basin aggregation does, and does not, unmark

At the root-composition level, (3.1) already aggregates all source
histories in the same M50 basin.  Thus there is one current per canonical
quotient edge, not one current per refinement history, and its quotient
energy is the additive quantity (3.4).

Disintegrating that current over the actual fine crossing edges is exact
at the refined endpoint because the forward merge rate is pointwise
constant.  At the coarse endpoint, however, its density relative to the
conditional stationary law is

```text
Pbar_s(y,F_refined)/R_s(coarse,refined),            (7.1)
```

which is generally nonconstant.  The residual of (7.1) is precisely the
right-heavy child (2.2).  Basin aggregation does not make this residual
zero.

The smallest exact witness is `s=3`: the root composition `(1,2)` merges
with probability one to unary macro `(0,1,2)`, whereas the stationary law
inside root composition `(3)` assigns masses `1/3,2/3` to
`(0,1,1),(0,1,2)`.  Even after aggregating all starting root degrees,
canonical coalescence has endpoint densities `15/16,33/32`, not one.
Therefore a recurrence which simply drops all quotient-reset children is
not an accounting identity.  One must either prove cancellation after
grouping the signed right-heavy residuals, or route their aggregate with a
polynomial actual-edge load.

There is a polynomial number of *current* labels in ambient rank `r`:
along a deep segment, `K` increases by the current inner root degree, and
the rank drop is at least that degree, so `K<=K_0+r`; also
`0<=R<K`, `1<=B<=r`, and the active root and last reset edge have only
polynomially many locations.  This observation alone is insufficient.
Cauchy--Schwarz applied anew at every depth would multiply the label count;
the required bound must group histories once, or use an occupation
identity such as (5.4).

## 8. Two falsification facts

First, `(k,last part)` is not a strong lumping of `G_s`.  At `s=5`, the
compositions `(1,3,1)` and `(2,2,1)` both have `(k,last)=(3,1)`, but their
aggregate split rates to `(k,last)=(4,1)` are respectively

```text
2w_1w_2/w_3=4/3,             2w_1w_1/w_2=2.        (8.1)
```

Thus the closed form for `H_x` does not reduce the Green problem to a
strongly lumped `(k,last)` chain.

Second, `canonical_marked_probe.py` evaluates the exact rank-acyclic
separated recurrence with (3.1).  With all `K<=8`, every `R,B`, and the
additional displayed `K` slices through `4096`, its largest values through
rank fourteen are

```text
s       2     3     4     5     6     7     8
max T  .444  1.145 1.764 2.533 3.157 3.676 4.155

s       9    10    11    12    13    14
max T  4.654 5.083 5.458 5.803 6.153 6.463.
```

This is compatible with polynomial, roughly linear growth.  It is a finite
falsifier only and still uses separate capacity copies for marked residuals.

## 9. Remaining standalone proposition

Let `D` be the exact deep kernel (H.4), and let `J_can` be the canonical
quotient-reset kernel whose coefficient on (2.2) is
`theta_x(e)^2/[Q_G(e)q_x]`.  Every row of `J_can` lands in the right-heavy
set, while (5.3) gives a `3/4` contraction for `D` in suffix-excess weight.
The remaining analytic statement is:

> **CANONICAL RIGHT-HEAVY RESET OCCUPATION.**  Prove that the rank-acyclic
> Green expansion generated by `D+J_can`, started from any ambient-feasible
> contextual mark, has total base cost at most a universal polynomial in
> the ambient rank.  Equivalently, control repeated applications of
> `(I-D)^(-1)J_can` on the right-heavy reset set.  Then group the resulting
> signed reset currents on actual `Pbar` edges with only one polynomial
> source-recovery loss.

Equations (2.3), (3.9), (5.3), and (6.2) prove all one-segment inputs to
this proposition.  Equation (7.1) and the `s=3` witness show why the reset
operator cannot simply be omitted.  No infinite obstruction that survives
unmarking is proved here, and no polynomial energy comparison for actual
unmarked `Pbar` is yet claimed.

