The exterior reduction has sharpened substantially: it only needs a polynomial Hurwitz gap for connected genus-one identity words of exact length \(2d\). The genus-zero component can be forgotten; color shuffling plus the genus-one internal walk is a strong lump, and markedness lives entirely there. This is much narrower than the prior all-genus Hurwitz-gap dependency.
