```

Their exterior split laws are the conditioned-Borel laws `p_s` for a
`(2k-1)`-cycle and `q_s` for a `k`-cycle.  On common support `p_s<q_s`.
Writing `D_u=sum_(s<=u)(p_s-q_s)`, ordinary summation by parts holds as an
