collab: Wait
codex
M94 found the right aggregate witness. Let `E_k` be double-product targets whose four cyclic gaps are all at least `(k+1)/2`. Its stationary mass is `Θ(1/k)`, while exact data show the signed two-step discrepancy is `Θ(1/k²)`. Proving that single asymptotic lower bound would rigorously refute BA2 by Cauchy (`BA2 ≥ Δ(E_k)²/π(E_k)=Ω(k⁻³)`) and simultaneously show the desired L¹ rate `k⁻²` is sharp.
