Let `r_k=(k+1)/2`.  Define `E_k` to consist of quotient double-transposition
states whose four positive cyclic support gaps `(x,y,z,w)` all satisfy

```text
x,y,z,w >= r_k.                                      (4.1)
```

Condition `(4.1)` is invariant under the four colored-composition encodings
of the same double orbit.

### Proposition 3 (proved: exact mass and `Theta(k^-1)` asymptotic)

The exact stationary mass is

```text
bar pi(E_k)=n(n-3)!/n^(n-2)
 sum_[x+y+z+w=n; x,y,z,w>=r_k]
       tau(x)tau(z)tau(y+w),                          (4.2)
```

where `tau(d)=d^(d-1)/d!`.  If `rho=1/6`, then

```text
k bar pi(E_k) -> I_rho/(6 pi),                        (4.3)

I_rho=integral_[x,y,z,w>=rho; x+y+z+w=1]
          [x z (y+w)]^(-3/2) dx dy dz,
```

and `0<I_rho<infinity`.  In particular there are absolute constants
`0<c_E<C_E<infinity` such that

```text
c_E/k <= bar pi(E_k) <= C_E/k                         (4.4)
```

for every sufficiently large odd `k`.

#### Proof

A colored positive four-composition has residual sizes

```text
S: (x,z,y+w),       N: (x+z,y,w).
```

Every odd-`n` double orbit has size `n` and exactly four colored-composition
encodings.  The `S` and `N` sums over the invariant domain `(4.1)` agree by
a cyclic change of variables.  Substituting M73's orbit mass

```text
n*2*(n-3)! tau(lambda_1)tau(lambda_2)tau(lambda_3)/n^(n-2)
```

and dividing the two-color encoding sum by four proves `(4.2)`.

Write the product in `(4.2)` as `e^n b_xb_zb_(y+w)`.  Stirling gives

```text
n(n-3)!e^n/n^(n-2) ~ sqrt(2 pi)n^(1/2).               (4.5)
```

The three Borel factors contribute
`(2 pi)^(-3/2)n^(-9/2)` uniformly on `(4.1)`, and the three-dimensional
lattice Riemann sum contributes `n^3`.  Since `r_k/n->1/6`, the product of
these factors is exactly `(2 pi n)^(-1) I_rho(1+o(1))`.  Replacing
`n=3k` proves `(4.3)`.  The integration domain is compact, has positive
volume, and stays away from every singular face, proving positivity,
finiteness, and `(4.4)`.  QED.

Equivalently, integrating first over `y` gives the explicit two-dimensional
form

```text
I_rho=integral_[x,z>=rho; x+z<=1-2rho]
 (1-x-z-2rho)[x z (1-x-z)]^(-3/2) dz dx.              (4.6)
```

## 5. A one-scalar route to refuting `(BA2)`

### Proposition 4 (proved: event lower bound and separation from L1)

For every odd `k>=3`,

```text
(BA2)_k >= Delta_k(E_k)^2/bar pi(E_k).                (5.1)
```

Consequently:

1. `(BA2)_k=O(k^-4)` implies
   `Delta_k(E_k)=O(k^-5/2)`;
2. if `liminf k^2 |Delta_k(E_k)|>0`, then
   `(BA2)_k=Omega(k^-3)`, so `(BA2)` is false;
3. the same lower bound on `Delta_k(E_k)` merely gives
   `TV>=|Delta_k(E_k)|=Omega(k^-2)` (up to the convention for signed TV),
   and therefore does **not** refute a matching direct `O(k^-2)` L1 bound.

#### Proof

Apply Cauchy--Schwarz on `E_k` to the signed density `z_k`:

```text
Delta_k(E_k)^2
 =[sum_(O_t in E_k)bar pi(O_t)z_k(O_t)]^2
 <=bar pi(E_k) sum_(O_t in E_k)bar pi(O_t)z_k(O_t)^2.
```

The last sum is at most `(BA2)_k`, proving `(5.1)`.  Combine it with
Proposition 3.  Total variation dominates the absolute signed mass of any
event, proving the final statement.  QED.

The remaining scalar statement is therefore:

> **CENTRAL DOUBLE BULK DEFECT `(BD)` (unresolved).**  There is an absolute
> `c>0` such that for all sufficiently large odd `k`,
>
> ```text
> |bar K^2(O_B,E_k)-bar K^2(O_A,E_k)| >= c/k^2.       (BD)
> ```

Unlike `(BA2)`, `(BD)` has no targetwise square, no rare stationary
denominator, and only one invariant event.  Equation `(2.8)` is its exact
signed Borel-convolution formula.  Proving `(BD)` would rigorously refute
`(BA2)` while leaving the desired direct signed-L1 estimate open.

## 6. Finite falsification evidence, not an asymptotic proof

The exact checker verifies `(4.2)` and `(5.1)` over `Fraction` at `k=3,5`.
The all-target floating diagnostic extends the scalar check to `k=7,9`.
The finite values are recorded in the report and JSON artifacts.  They show
stable positive `k^2 Delta_k(E_k)` near `0.04` and stable
`k bar pi(E_k)` near `0.07` from `k=5` onward, but they cannot prove `(BD)`.

The strongest self-attack is that the signed convolution `(2.8)` still has
large cancellation across intermediate residual shells.  At the central
`k=7` targets, the minimum-one double-intermediate shell is negative while
the minimum-two through minimum-six shells are positive.  No termwise
positivity or monotonicity needed for `(BD)` has yet been proved.

## 7. A direct-L1 shell envelope that may survive `(BA2)`

Let

```text
S_d={O_t: min cycle size of t^-1 h equals d},          1<=d<=k,
M_(k,d)=bar pi(S_d),
Z_(k,d)=sup_(O_t in S_d)|z_k(O_t)|.                  (7.1)
```

### Proposition 5 (proved: sufficient shell criterion)

The direct signed target follows from the single summability condition

```text
sum_(d=1)^k M_(k,d) Z_(k,d) <= C/k^2.                (L1-shell)
```

More generally, it is enough to replace the supremum by the conditional
mean absolute score on each shell.  In contrast, `(BA2)` asks for

```text
sum_d M_(k,d) E[z_k^2 | S_d] <= C/k^4.                (7.2)
```

#### Proof

The shells partition the target space, so `(2.5)` gives

```text
2 TV=sum_d M_(k,d)E[|z_k| | S_d]
    <=sum_d M_(k,d)Z_(k,d).
```

The analogous decomposition of the square gives `(7.2)`.  QED.

This is elementary but cleanly displays the exponent separation.  The
stationary minimum-residual law has the conditioned-Borel boundary envelope

```text
M_(k,d) <= C d^(-3/2)                                (7.3)
```

away from the final balanced cutoff; `(7.3)` follows by the same coefficient
extraction/Stirling argument as M73's residual-composition formulas.  More
explicitly, fixing one residual component at `d` leaves a two-Borel
convolution of total size `n-d`.  For doubles, the extra number of ways to
split the third component is at most linear in its size; the Borel--Tanner
identity cancels that linear factor against the `n^(-1/2)` normalization.
Thus every choice of the minimum contributes at most `C b_d`, and
`b_d<=C d^(-3/2)`.  Triangles have no linear splitting factor and are
smaller.  A union bound over the three component choices proves `(7.3)`.
The
finite score shells suggest the complementary envelope

```text
Z_(k,d) <= C d/k,                                    (7.4)
```

but `(7.3)--(7.4)` alone sum only to `O(k^-1/2)`, far too weak.  The target
scale requires substantial signed posterior cancellation inside each shell,
not just a pointwise likelihood bound.  The boundary and positive-volume
bulk have different natural scales.  A falsifiable sufficient form retaining
both is

```text
M_(k,d) E[|z_k| | S_d]
 <= C/k^2 * [d^(-3/2)+(kd)^(-1/2)]                  (L1-envelope)
```

uniformly for `1<=d<=k`.  Indeed `sum_d d^(-3/2)=O(1)` and
`sum_(d<=k)(kd)^(-1/2)=O(1)`, so it proves `(L1-shell)`.  The first term is
the small-component boundary envelope; for `d=Theta(k)`, the second is
`Theta(k^-1)` after the outside `k^-2`, matching a positive-volume bulk
distributed across `Theta(k)` shells.  Exact values at `k=7,9` satisfy this
shape with small finite constants, but they only calibrate it.
`(L1-envelope)` is **unresolved**, and no direct L1 upper bound is claimed.

The central event from Proposition 3 has mass `Theta(k^-1)` and average
score empirically `Theta(k^-1)`, so it naturally contributes
`Theta(k^-2)` to L1 but `Theta(k^-3)` to L2.  This makes the scalar bulk
obstruction compatible with `(L1-envelope)` only at its summability edge,
exactly as required.
# M94 report: central-double obstruction to balanced `(BA2)`

Date: 2026-08-12. Repository base commit:
`502a6f031c6d5a4bc0064ee5b370a4fa3914f993`.

## 1. Exact claim, quantifiers, convention, scope, and status

Permutations compose as `(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`; tuple factors multiply
left-to-right.  Fix `n=3k`, with odd `k>=3`, and

```text
h=(0 1 ... n-1),
A_k=(0,k,2k),       B_k=(0,1)(k,2k).
```

The target is uniform on minimal length-`n-1` transposition factorizations
of `h`.  `bar K` is M73's nonlazy rank-two pair-product kernel modulo cyclic
conjugation by `h`; it is not the identity-word heat-bath kernel.

M91's balanced collision inequality

```text
(BA2)_k=||bar K(eta_k/bar pi)||_(2,bar pi)^2=O(k^-4),
eta_k=bar K(B_k,.)-bar K(A_k,.),
```

remains **unresolved**, but this report produces a sharply targeted
obstruction.  It proves:

1. an exact signed Borel-convolution formula for the complete two-step score;
2. sharp bulk and boundary asymptotics for M91's Abel coefficients;
3. an invariant central-double event `E_k` with exact stationary mass and
   `bar pi(E_k)=Theta(k^-1)`; and
4. the implication

```text
liminf k^2 |bar K^2(B_k,E_k)-bar K^2(A_k,E_k)|>0
   => (BA2)_k=Omega(k^-3),                            (1.1)
```

which would refute `(BA2)` but is compatible with direct signed
`L1=O(k^-2)`.

The scalar premise in `(1.1)`, called `(BD)` below, is **unresolved**.
No `(BA2)` refutation, direct L1 upper bound, general strict-edge estimate,
H0 gap, bridge gap, identity heat-bath gap, or Terminal conclusion is claimed.

## 2. Exact target-residual/Borel convolution

Put

```text
b_d=e^-d d^(d-1)/d!,
beta_3(x)=product_(C cycle of x^-1 h)b_|C|,
beta_5(x,y)=1[ell_T((xy)^-1h)=n-5]
              product_(C cycle of (xy)^-1h)b_|C|,
R_n=(n-3)(n-4),
c_n=(n-3)!e^n/n^(n-2).
```

Singleton cycles are included.  M73's exact completion counts become

```text
pi(x)=a(x)c_n beta_3(x),
K(x,y)=a(y)/R_n * beta_5(x,y)/beta_3(x),              (2.1)
```

where `a=3` for triangles and `a=2` for doubles.

Define the complete signed first-row defect

```text
d_k(s)=beta_5(B_k,s)/beta_3(B_k)
       -beta_5(A_k,s)/beta_3(A_k).                    (2.2)
```

For a target orbit `O_t`, let

```text
Q_t(s)=|O_t|^-1 sum_(t' in O_t)beta_5(s,t').          (2.3)
```

Directly expanding the intermediate quotient orbit gives the proved exact
posterior score

```text
z_k(O_t):=[bar K^2(O_B,O_t)-bar K^2(O_A,O_t)]/bar pi(O_t)

=1/[c_n R_n^2 beta_3(t)]
  sum_(s in X_n)a(s)d_k(s)Q_t(s)/beta_3(s).           (2.4)
```

The factor `|O_t|` in `(2.3)` retains every cyclic stabilizer, including the
size-`k` orbit of `A_k`.  Every triangle/double micro-lift remains in `a`.
The quotient and raw norms agree because `z_k` is orbit-invariant:

```text
(BA2)_k=E_pi[z_k^2],       2 TV=E_pi|z_k|.            (2.5)
```

For any invariant raw target event `E`, the target sum collapses exactly to

```text
Delta_k(E):=bar K^2(O_B,E)-bar K^2(O_A,E)

=1/R_n^2 sum_s a(s)d_k(s)/beta_3(s)
        sum_(t in E)a(t)beta_5(s,t).                  (2.6)
```

Equation `(2.6)` retains both M91 channels and all second-row schemas before
any estimate.  It is not a channelwise triangle bound.

## 3. Proved Abel and central-event asymptotics

For M91's split laws `p_s,q_s` and cumulative difference
`D_u=sum_(s<=u)(p_s-q_s)`, define

```text
P(x)=(2 pi)^(-1/2)x^(-3/2)(1-x/2)^(-3/2),
Q(x)=(2 pi)^(-1/2)x^(-3/2)(1-x)^(-3/2)1[x<1/2],
mathcal D(x)=integral_0^x(P-Q).
```

Uniform Stirling bounds and a boundary/bulk split prove

```text
sqrt(k)D_floor(kx) -> mathcal D(x)     (0<x<1, x!=1/2),

D_u ~ -3/[2 sqrt(2 pi)] sqrt(u)/k
                    (u->infinity, u=o(k)).            (3.1)
```

Thus the Abel weights genuinely retain a `k^-1/2` bulk scale.

Let `r_k=(k+1)/2`, and let `E_k` be the double-target orbits whose four
positive cyclic support gaps `(x,y,z,w)` all satisfy `>=r_k`.  This is
well-defined under all four colored encodings.  Its exact mass is

```text
bar pi(E_k)=n(n-3)!/n^(n-2)
 sum_[x+y+z+w=n; x,y,z,w>=r_k]
      tau(x)tau(z)tau(y+w),                           (3.2)
```

with `tau(d)=d^(d-1)/d!`.  A three-dimensional uniform Stirling/Riemann
calculation proves

```text
k bar pi(E_k) -> I/(6 pi),                            (3.3)

I=integral_[x,y,z,w>=1/6; x+y+z+w=1]
      [x z (y+w)]^(-3/2) dx dy dz,
```

where `0<I<infinity`.  Hence `bar pi(E_k)=Theta(k^-1)`.

## 4. Probability, multiplicity, runtime, and cancellation accounting

- `bar K` is the exact nonlazy quotient correlation kernel for the uniform
  minimal long-cycle bridge.
- All exact formulas use literal raw lift multiplicity and distinct cyclic
  orbit size.  No generic size-`n` substitution is made for `O_A`.
- The Borel rewrite is an algebraic identity:
  `F_r(q)=r!e^n product_C b_|C|` when the cycle sizes sum to `n`.
- `E_k` is invariant, so its four colored double-composition encodings are
  divided out exactly in `(3.2)`.
- The square in `(BA2)` and absolute value in TV occur after the complete
  signed convolution `(2.4)`; the `J=1,2` channels are never bounded
  separately.
- Exact `k=3,5` checks use Python `Fraction`; floating `k<=11` checks use
  NumPy `1.26.4`.  All are deterministic (`seed=null`) under Python
  `3.12.3`.

## 5. Dependencies and status labels

- **Accepted proved input (M73/M80):** raw and quotient rank-two kernels,
  orbit masses, reversibility, cyclic composition parameterization, and the
  `I3,IS,IN,X` row schemas.
- **Accepted proved input (M83/M88):** the balanced strict edge, its residual
  cycles, and conditioned-Borel split law.
- **Accepted proved input (M91/M93):** posterior score, common `J=0`
  cancellation, normalized `J=1,2` laws, the measure-valued Abel identity,
  and equivalence of `(BA2)` to the localized stationary L2 contrast.
- **Proved here:** `(2.4)--(2.6)`, Abel scaling `(3.1)`, exact event mass
  `(3.2)`, the positive finite limit `(3.3)`, stationary Cauchy obstruction
  `(1.1)`, and the exact L1 shell decomposition below.
- **Exact finite only:** central-event formulas and Cauchy lower bound at
  `k=3,5`.
- **Floating finite only:** shell, channel, and event values through `k=11`.
- **Unresolved:** `(BD)`, `(BA2)`, the balanced direct L1 upper bound, the
  general strict edge, H0, and all sampler-gap/Terminal consequences.

No external literature theorem is added by this mission.

## 6. First unproved standalone obligations

The sharp refutation target is now one scalar:

> **CENTRAL DOUBLE BULK DEFECT `(BD)` (unresolved).**  There is an absolute
> `c>0` such that for all sufficiently large odd `k`,
>
> ```text
> |Delta_k(E_k)|>=c/k^2.                              (BD)
> ```

Stationary Cauchy--Schwarz gives, exactly,

```text
(BA2)_k >= Delta_k(E_k)^2/bar pi(E_k).                (6.1)
```

Together with `(3.3)`, `(BD)` proves `(BA2)_k=Omega(k^-3)` and therefore
refutes `(BA2)`.  Yet TV only satisfies `TV>=|Delta_k(E_k)|=Omega(k^-2)`,
so direct `O(k^-2)` remains possible.

M91's Abel identity sharpens `(BD)` without channel splitting.  Write the
complete event defect as

```text
Delta_k(E_k)=Gradient_k+Embedding_k,                  (6.2)
```

where both terms already combine `alpha_1` and `alpha_2`; `Gradient_k` is
the sum with coefficients `D_u`, and `Embedding_k` is the sum with
coefficients `q_s`.  A sufficient next proof is

```text
liminf k^2 Embedding_k > limsup k^2 |Gradient_k|.     (6.3)
```

Finite values at `k=5,7` are respectively

```text
k^2 Embedding_k:   0.05583,  0.05149,
k^2 Gradient_k:   -0.00874, -0.00829.
```

Every finite embedding split is positive in these checks, while gradient
splits have both signs.  This only identifies the proof interface; it does
not establish `(6.3)` asymptotically.

For the weaker direct L1 route, let `S_d` be the target shell with minimum
residual cycle size `d`, and let `z_k` be `(2.4)`.  The exact partition is

```text
2 TV=sum_(d=1)^k bar pi(S_d)E[|z_k| | S_d].           (6.4)
```

A falsifiable sufficient boundary-plus-bulk envelope is

```text
bar pi(S_d)E[|z_k| | S_d]
 <=C/k^2 [d^(-3/2)+(kd)^(-1/2)].                     (L1-envelope)
```

Both terms sum uniformly in `d`; this would prove direct `O(k^-2)`.  It is
unresolved.

