A_k=(0,k,2k),       B_k=(0,1)(k,2k),
eta=bar K(B_k,.)-bar K(A_k,.),
f=eta/bar pi,
```

reversibility gives the exact posterior score

```text
f(s)=bar K(s,B_k)/bar pi(B_k)-bar K(s,A_k)/bar pi(A_k),
eta bar K(t)=bar pi(t)(bar K f)(t).                (L-0214.1)
```

The cyclic phase formula in `(L-0214.1)` retains the exceptional orbit size
`|O_A|=k`, the free orbit size `|O_B|=n`, and every ordered-pair lift.  After
conditioning the first two completion factors by their residual-component
colors, the identical `J=0` middle-`k`-cycle law cancels exactly.  The two
remaining channels have coefficients

```text
alpha_1=4(k-1)^2/[(3k-3)(3k-4)],
alpha_2=2(k-1)(2k-3)/[(3k-3)(3k-4)].              (L-0214.2)
```

Their exterior split laws are the conditioned-Borel laws `p_s` for a
`(2k-1)`-cycle and `q_s` for a `k`-cycle.  On common support `p_s<q_s`.
Writing `D_u=sum_(s<=u)(p_s-q_s)`, ordinary summation by parts holds as an
exact identity of signed measures:

```text
H_(j,B)-H_(j,A)
 =sum_(u=1)^(k-2)D_u(Phi_(j,u)-Phi_(j,u+1))
  +sum_(s=1)^((k-1)/2)q_s(Phi_(j,s)-Psi_(j,s)).   (L-0214.3)
```

All conditional measures in `(L-0214.3)` are normalized before projecting
to cyclic product orbits.  The cumulative coefficients are negative through
`k-2`, have maximum magnitude `Theta(k^-1/2)`, and total absolute weight
asymptotic to `[(2-sqrt(2))/sqrt(pi)]sqrt(k)`.  Thus Abel summation exposes,
but does not itself supply, the further smoothing required after the second
kernel.

The remaining positive inequality is the single channel-combined statement

```text
E_barpi[alpha_1 A_(1,k)(t)+alpha_2 A_(2,k)(t)]^2
 <=C/k^4.                                         (BA2)
```

Equivalently its left side is

```text
||bar K f||_2^2
 =bar K^4(B,B)/bar pi(B)+bar K^4(A,A)/bar pi(A)
  -bar K^4(A,B)/bar pi(B)-bar K^4(B,A)/bar pi(A). (L-0214.4)
```

BA2 would imply the balanced two-step total-variation bound `O(k^-2)` by
one stationary Cauchy--Schwarz inequality.  It remains unproved and is
stronger than the required signed-L1 estimate.  The full post-kernel `J=1`
