It works at `N>=5,m=2N-2` in one two-component minimal exterior macro
`Gamma`, whose unique positive-genus component has genus one.  For the
declared lazy physical signed-Hurwitz walk, if

```text
inf_(x in Gamma) Pr_x(tau_G<=T)>=a,
```

then choosing a uniform random time in `{0,...,T}` and sampling that many
walk proposals gives a source-independent law on fixed bijective signed
words with endpoint mark probability at least `a/(T+1)` and expected emitted
length `T/4`.  M75/M77 first-crossing recovery therefore gives every
`S subseteq Gamma` the literal actual-edge bound

```text
sum_(x in S) K(x,(Gamma\S) union (F_N\A))
 >=p_H a|S|/[(T+1)max(T/4,1)],
p_H=1/[6(m-2)binom(N,2)^2].                         (L-0216.1)
```

The crucial new reduction projects a macro state to its binary color
interleaving and the internal word of the genus-one component, forgetting
the genus-zero word.  This is a pointwise strong lump: genus-one/genus-one
proposals are internal Hurwitz moves, mixed proposals swap disjoint colors,
and genus-zero/genus-zero proposals become self-loops.  Every projection
fiber has the same omitted-word multiplicity, the projected stationary law
is the product of uniform color and genus-one laws, and the M75 marked set is
projection-measurable.

Let `gamma_1(d)` be the gap of the half-lazy signed adjacent-Hurwitz walk on
connected identity words of length `2d` on a fixed labeled `d`-set.  The
accepted M05 shuttle paths use only the retained coordinates and give

```text
gap(Pbar_Gamma)>=gamma_1(d)/(2m^9)
                   >=gamma_1(d)/m^10.               (L-0216.2)
```

Together with the accepted marked density
`zeta>=3/[Nm(m-1)]`, ordinary finite-state mixing turns any inverse-
polynomial lower bound for `gamma_1(d)` into an inverse-polynomial
source-independent marked-word law and then `(L-0216.1)`.  No gap for the
genus-zero component is needed.  The still narrower sufficient proposition
is a uniform polynomial worst-source hitting time of the marked set itself.
Both propositions remain open.  Under the current repository guide,
Classification H/transitivity is conditional pending source/convention
verification; neither positive reduction uses it, because a positive
`gamma_1` or the hitting hypothesis already supplies the required
reachability.

M92 also proves exact limits of canonical alternatives.  Every genus-one
factorization torus has a tree--cotree certificate with exactly two leftover
edges whose fundamental cycles form an integral homology basis, but an exact
`S_4`, length-eight collision shows that the leftover positions and labels
do not determine the required tree path.  More globally, for every labeled
