### L-0219 - Genus-one Hurwitz walk has an exact spectrum-preserving handle cut

M97 freezes report SHA-256
`73ab5bec4d5ba48bb1b4511099df056525fe1f6b6f1b6caa6f79b7964feb3c99`
and manifest SHA-256
`6d0c28f8a4414175a3226b77fb1cff3217599f14ad707eaf5a7d3e3470babc4f`.
For the half-lazy signed adjacent-Hurwitz walk `P_d` on uniform connected
identity words of length `2d` on fixed labels `[d]`, define prefix genus

```text
g(u)=[length(u)-d-cycles(eval(u))+2 support_components(u)]/2.
```

Appending a transposition changes `g` by zero or one.  Every full genus-one
word has unique forward and backward handle positions `h(w),b(w)` with
`b(w)<h(w)`.  At every cut `j` in the nonempty interval
`J(w)={b(w),...,h(w)-1}`, both sides are componentwise genus zero.  Their
bipartite support-partition incidence graph has one edge per cycle of the
cut permutation and is connected unicyclic.  Connectivity is exactly the
condition that the left/right support partitions have one-block join.

The lifted law and kernel

```text
tilde pi(w,j)=pi_d(w)/|J(w)|,
L((w,j),(w',j'))=P_d(w,w')/|J(w')|
```

are exact.  With cut averaging `R` and word lifting `U`, `L=UP_dR` and
`RU=I`, so

```text
spec(L)=spec(P_d) plus zeros,       gap(L)=gap(P_d).              (L-0219.1)
```

This is an everywhere-defined coordinate decomposition, not a gap proof.
It avoids the exact zero fibers of literal connected-square deletion.  The
handle coordinate alone is neither a strong lump nor pointwise mobile: an
explicit family has fixed `h=3` under every one-step proposal for all
`d>=3`.  Marked deletion instead has density proportional to the mark count
and vanishes on the accepted M92 tree-indexed unmarked family.

M101 independently ACCEPTS with zero material objection.  It exhausts all
`1,181,045` cuts through `d=4`, verifies the tree/unicycle profiles,
componentwise genera, strict `b<h`, local handle motion, and insertion/
deletion multiplicity.  At `d=3` it reconstructs the 240-state base and
336-state lift, finds exactly 96 added zero eigenvalues, and matches the gap
and `L=UP_dR`.  It also checks the frozen-handle family through `d=12` and
the M92 unmarked family through all labeled trees at `d=5`.  M101 report
SHA-256 is
`e129ea085bf10679056bee55186ec2c3382e4d192459adb90585a20a3b1635a3`;
