`f36a625702a7b93dbebabc3ded4edcfda326ba3c85dae244bb52ed92ab8412f9`.
For M97's exact spectrum-preserving central-cut lift, condition on the
realizable seam key

```text
kappa=(j,p,Q_L,Q_R).
```

The raw cell is literally a product `C_kappa=U_kappa x V_kappa` of two
componentwise genus-zero factorization/interleaving spaces.  If `D=2d-1`,
the lifted conditional law is the exact `1/ell` tilt of that product, with
density in `[D^-1,D]`.  The correct side variables are

```text
r_L(u)=j-b(uv)+1,       r_R(v)=h(uv)-j,
ell(u,v)=r_L(u)+r_R(v)-1,
1/ell=integral_0^1 z^(r_L-1) z^(r_R-1) dz.            (L-0222.1)
```

Wholly internal signed Hurwitz moves preserve the key; a nontrivial seam
move leaves it.  Stationary edge-flow and variance comparisons therefore
lose at most `D^3` between the raw and lifted restrictions.  Re-specializing
the accepted M05 shuttle with exactly two side-color slots gives

```text
gap(P_kappa)>=Gamma_0(d)/(420D^10),
gap(L_kappa)>=Gamma_0(d)/(420D^13).                    (L-0222.2)
```

Here `Gamma_0(d)` is the worst gap among the connected componentwise
genus-zero signed-Hurwitz coordinates actually occurring in a seam cell; it
is unresolved.  If `beta(d)` is the gap of the exact stationary-flow cell
projection, a direct restriction/projection variance decomposition gives

```text
gamma_1(d)>=Gamma_0(d) beta(d)/(2940D^13).             (L-0222.3)
```

Both factors on the right remain open.  The decisive self-attack is the
realizable cell

```text
C_(kappa_e)=Z_d x {(e,e)},
Z_d={connected identity words on [d] of length 2d-2},
P_(kappa_e)=((D-2)/D)P_(0,d)+(2/D)I.                  (L-0222.4)
```

Thus standard fixed-cell tensorization reintroduces the full-label minimal
genus-zero Hurwitz gap at the same `d`; it is not an induction.

