### L-0076 - Two natural full-support cuts have polynomial full-K boundary

The Cycle-05 M13 red team proves a halfway rejection of two further
Terminal-B candidates.  At `m=2N-2`, let `F_N` be the entire minimal
full-support macro.  Exact adjacent leaf-square insertion/deletion gives a
nonzero removable leaf square with probability at least `1/(8N)` under its
uniform law.  One boundary-safe padded `H_3` refresh then exits `F_N`, with
the full lazy scan normalization retained, so

    Q_K(F_N,F_N^c)
      >= pi(F_N)/[16 |R_m| N(m-2)M^2].

This lower-bounds the two-sided conductance by the same inverse polynomial,
regardless of which side is smaller.  The exact macro mass uses
`|F_N|=(2N-2)!N^(N-3)` divided by the full character-sum bridge count.

For every feasible length, the cut defined by a star at the first join has
exact mass `2/N` and outward conductance at least
`1/[2|R_m|(m-2)M^2]`.  Exact full `r=3,4,5` flow and reversibility checks pass
the `S_3,m=4`, `S_4,m=4`, and `S_4,m=6` calibrations.  The agent is still
auditing the formal report and the remaining embedded nonnormal-Schreier
candidate.

