    pi(F_N)=(2N-2)! N^(N-3)
      / [(1/N!) sum_lambda (f^lambda)^2 c_lambda^(2N-2)].

The trivial and sign representations give an explicit geometric upper bound
showing `pi(F_N)<1/2` for every `N>=6`.  Thus `F_N` is not merely a cut whose
