### L-0078 - A balanced temporal-articulation cut also has polynomial boundary

The M17 continuation tests a genuinely internal, exponentially rare cut rather
than another support macro.  For odd `N=2s+1` and `m=4s`, let `A` consist of
words whose two length-`2s` halves are minimal connected identity words on
supports of size `s+1`, with the two supports covering `[N]` and meeting in
exactly one articulation label.  Exact deletion/counting gives

    |A|=(2s+1) binom(2s,s)
        [(2s)! (s+1)^(s-2)]^2,

and the character formula supplies its exact global mass.  Conditional on the
minimal full-support macro, the mass is asymptotic to
`(8 sqrt(2)e/s)16^(-s)` and is at most `1/4`, so the orientation is explicit.

