The Duchi--Poulalhon--Schaeffer bijection is exactly measure-preserving at the
fully indexed level: face `i` records factor `t_i`, and Proposition 1 maps
uniform `Z_d` to uniform indexed increasing quadrangulations.  A Hurwitz move
on `t_i,t_(i+1)` therefore changes only the transpositions attached to two
consecutive face labels algebraically, but reconstructing the embedded
quadrangulation uses the global minimal `1-1` orientation and closure
algorithm.  The source proves a bijection and perfect sampler, not a local
intertwining.  No theorem in it says that a Hurwitz generator is a bounded
number of map flips/rotations or an adjacent label swap on a fixed map.

The Caraceni polynomial-gap chain acts on uniform unindexed rooted planar maps,
