algorithm.  The source proves a bijection and perfect sampler, not a local
intertwining.  No theorem in it says that a Hurwitz generator is a bounded
number of map flips/rotations or an adjacent label swap on a fixed map.

The Caraceni polynomial-gap chain acts on uniform unindexed rooted planar maps,
not uniform indexed increasing quadrangulations; forgetting indices has
nonconstant fibers.  Consequently the nonrecursive bypass remains exactly:

> **INDEXED HURWITZ-TREE LOCAL COMPARISON.**  Define a reversible
> inverse-polynomial-gap chain on uniform indexed increasing quadrangulations
> and simulate each of its moves by signed adjacent-Hurwitz moves with
> polynomial congestion (or conversely dominate it in Dirichlet form).

No such local translation or congestion proof is established here.  Thus the
bijection is a promising exact coordinate system, not a completed gap proof.

