The minimal-genus lane is now frozen for independent review. Its strongest new coordinate result is exact: after adjoining a white root, the difficult identity-word law becomes a product of a uniform spanning tree and a uniform permutation, and that ideal product chain has a standard polynomial gap. The remaining theorem is precisely a local path comparison back to signed Hurwitz moves; the report does not claim that comparison.
