# Exact marked-context inheritance

Date: 2026-08-12.  This note concerns only contextual split statistics in
the nonlazy minimal-long-cycle parking projection.  It is not a statement
about the identity-bridge chain `K`.

## 1. Synthetic attachment contexts

Fix a selected root branch and retain only the ordered root-attachment
factors relevant to its positional split weight.  Write

```text
O_1<...<O_K
```

for this external attachment chain, with active factor `O_(R+1)`; thus
`R` attachments precede the active factor.  The other branches may be
taken to be unit branches: multiset-word deletion gives the same local
statistic after the outside orbit and scan factors are divided out.  Denote
the resulting normalized local statistic by `Phi_(K,R;B)`.

Inside the selected branch, condition on root composition

```text
C=(c_1,...,c_k),        t=c_k,
```

and write `I_1<...<I_k` for its attachment chain, with `I_1` the
rightmost/last-branch attachment.  Deleting all other factors from a
uniform parking-multiset word leaves a uniform shuffle of the two chains
`O` and `I`.

## 2. Negative-hypergeometric recursion

Let `J` be the number of `I` factors preceding `O_(R+1)`.  Exactly `j`
inner and `R` outer factors occur before the active outer factor.  Hence

```text
nu_(K,R,k)(j)
 =P(J=j)
 =binom(R+j,j) binom(K-R-1+k-j,k-j)/binom(K+k,k),   (2.1)
```

for `0<=j<=k`.

**Theorem (marked inheritance).**  If `t>B` and `v` is the standardized
macro of the last inner branch, then pointwise in `v`,

```text
Phi_(K,R;B)(u)
 =sum_(j=1)^k nu_(K,R,k)(j)
      Phi_(K+k,R+j;B)(v).                           (2.2)
```

The child statistics on the right are synthetic attachment contexts; they
need not be actual root-composition contexts of the same ambient tree.

### Proof

Expose the two attachment chains in the constrained-shuffle bijection.
Every binary shuffle has the same number of inverse insertions of the
deleted factors.  If `J=0`, the active factor precedes `I_1`; the
right-spine cut factor inside the last branch cannot form the marked
favourable pair, so this class contributes zero.

Fix `J=j>=1`.  Delete every current-level factor outside the last branch,
but retain its attachment factor as a dummy unit-branch attachment.  The
result has `K+k` external attachment factors.  Exactly `R+j` precede the
same active factor.  Conversely, from a marked word in this synthetic
`(K+k,R+j)` context and a two-chain shuffle with `J=j`, insert the deleted
branch words in their recorded gaps.  Chain order, the marked scan site,
and the favourable rank-two outcome recover both the source and the
shuffle uniquely.

Thus deletion and insertion are inverse on marked favourable
word/outcome pairs.  Dividing by source-orbit size, the three-state fibre,
the scan count, and the corresponding `alpha` leaves precisely the binary
shuffle fraction (2.1).  Summing over `j>=1` proves (2.2).  No scalar
replacement by one ordinary child context has been made.

Vandermonde's identity gives

```text
sum_(j=1)^k nu_(K,R,k)(j)
 =1-nu_(K,R,k)(0)
 =1-binom(K,R+1)/binom(K+k,R+1)
 =D_(K,R)(k).                                       (2.3)
```

Every synthetic child context has stationary mean
`w_(t-B)w_B/w_t`, by the exact root-composition split flow.  Averaging
(2.2) and using (2.3) proves the deep line of the closed conditional-mean
formula.

## 3. Why `(k,0)` is false

The tempting replacement

```text
Phi_parent =D_(K,R)(k) Phi_(k,0)
```

is false first at ambient `r=4`.  Take parent context
`K=1,R=0`, coarse `(4)`, refinement `(3,1)`, and inner composition
`C=(3)`.  On the two last-branch macros `(0,0)` and `(0,1)`, the parent
values are both `1/3`.  The ordinary child `(1,0)` values are `1` and
`1/2`, so multiplication by `D=1/2` predicts `1/2` and `1/4`.

Equation (2.2) instead has `j=1`, weight `1/2`, and synthetic child
`(K',R')=(2,1)`.  That child has values `2/3,2/3`, giving the correct
`1/3,1/3`.

`context_map_audit.py` records the scalar failure.  The corrected
`marked_context_inheritance_audit.py` has zero mismatches in all
`898=1+7+36+163+691` nonvacuous exact checks through ambient `r=7`.
These computations are falsifiers only; the proof is the marked
deletion/insertion bijection above.

## 4. Repeated extreme geometry

The update does not force a rightmost (`R=0`) child context.  If
`R=K-1` and `j=k`, then

```text
(K',R')=(K+k,K+k-1),

nu_k=binom(K-1+k,k)/binom(K+k,k)=K/(K+k).           (4.1)
```

Thus the same extreme geometry repeats with probability weight close to
one when `K>>k`.  Along a unary spine (`k=1`) the depth-`d` continuation
weight telescopes exactly:

```text
product_(h=0)^(d-1) (K+h)/(K+h+1)=K/(K+d).         (4.2)
```

It is only polynomially suppressed and is essentially unsuppressed for
`d<<K`.  Hence an arbitrary-context quotient cost cannot be declared a
one-time loss.  Any surviving proof must carry the full marked mixture
and its edge loads, not only conditional means or the pair `(k,0)`.
# Exact contextual conditional-mean formula

Date: 2026-08-12.  This note concerns only the nonlazy minimal-long-cycle
parking projection.  It does not concern the identity-bridge chain `K`.
Permutations compose as `(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`, and factor tuples multiply
left-to-right.

## 1. Statement

Fix an outer root composition with `K>=1` branches and split its branch
`i` into a left part and a suffix of size `B>=1`.  Let

```text
R=K-i-1
```

be the number of outer branches to the right of the split branch.  In the
standardized split branch, condition on the inner root composition

```text
C=(c_1,...,c_k),       t=c_k.
```

Let `phi` be the contextual split rate divided by
`alpha_r=2/[3r(r-1)]`, and put

```text
w_a=a^(a-1)/a!.
```

**Theorem (closed contextual mean).**  For every ambient rank, every
outer context above, and every feasible inner composition,

```text
E[phi | C] = 0,                                      t<B,

E[phi | C] = T_(K,R)(k),                            t=B,

E[phi | C] = [w_(t-B)w_B/w_t] D_(K,R)(k),           t>B,       (1.1)
```

where

```text
T_(K,R)(k)
 =K binom(k+K-R-2,K-R-1)/binom(k+K-1,K-1),          (1.2)

D_(K,R)(k)
 =1-binom(K,R+1)/binom(K+k,R+1).                    (1.3)
```

Thus the conditional mean depends on the outer context only through
`(K,R)`, and on the inner composition only through `(k,t)`.

## 2. Uniform two-chain deletion lemma

For a fixed parking macro, Stanley--Biane identifies its factor words
with all permutations of its lower-endpoint multiset.  Occurrences of a
vertex label are the attachment factors of its ordered children, in the
reverse child order.  Consequently, after deleting every factor except
the `K` outer-root attachments and the `k` inner-root attachments, the
remaining word is a uniformly random shuffle of two ordered chains

```text
O_1<...<O_K,       I_1<...<I_k.                     (2.1)
```

Here `O_(R+1)` is the attachment of the outer branch being split and
`I_1` is the attachment of its last inner root branch.  The positions of
the `K+k` retained factors among all `r` factor positions are uniform and
independent of their binary order.  Hence any fixed adjacent pair in the
binary restriction is adjacent in the full word with probability

```text
(K+k)/r.                                            (2.2)
```

These statements remain true after fixing all other branch macros:
deletion has the same number of inverse insertions for every binary word.
This is also the direct multiset-word version of the constrained-shuffle
bijection used in M56.

## 3. Terminal count `t=B`

At equality, the cut factor is `I_1`.  The two coarse rank-two outcomes
put `O_(R+1)` and `I_1` in the two possible orders.  They are adjacent in
the binary restriction precisely when it starts with either

```text
O^R O I       or       O^R I O.
```

After this displayed prefix is removed, the remaining word has `k-1`
inner and `K-R-1` outer letters.  Therefore the number of favourable
binary words is

```text
2 binom(k+K-R-2,K-R-1),                             (3.1)
```

out of `binom(K+k,K)`.

For each favourable word, (2.2) gives full-word adjacency.  The scan
selects that site with probability `1/(r-1)`, and the exact three-state
rank-two heat bath selects the split outcome with probability `1/3`.
After division by `alpha_r`, the normalized rate is

```text
[r/2] [(K+k)/r]
 [2 binom(k+K-R-2,K-R-1)/binom(K+k,K)]

=K binom(k+K-R-2,K-R-1)/binom(k+K-1,K-1),
```

which is (1.2).  This calculation retains both coarse orientations and
does not add an extra factor two for the single split target.

## 4. Deep count `t>B`

Now the marked cut factor lies strictly inside the last inner branch.
Let `J` be the number of inner attachment factors which precede
`O_(R+1)` in the uniform two-chain shuffle.  A marked opportunity can
continue into the last branch exactly when

```text
I_1 precedes O_(R+1), equivalently J>=1.            (4.1)
```

Conditionally on `J=j>=1`, marked deletion and insertion identify the
last-branch statistic with a synthetic child attachment context having
`K+k` attachments and `R+j` before the same active factor.  The exact
negative-hypergeometric weights and pointwise recursion are proved in
`marked_context_inheritance.md`.  In particular this is a mixture of child
contexts, not a scalar multiple of the ordinary `(k,0)` child.

The complement of (4.1) says that the first `R+1` symbols of the uniform
binary shuffle are all outer symbols.  Sampling these symbols without
replacement gives

```text
P(I_1 precedes O_(R+1))
 =1-(K)_(R+1)/(K+k)_(R+1)
 =1-binom(K,R+1)/binom(K+k,R+1).                    (4.2)
```

Every synthetic child context has the same stationary mean: summing its
marked opportunities is exactly the stationary-flow split from the
one-part composition `(t)` to `(t-B,B)`.  M50's exact reverse root-split
formula says that its rate divided by the relevant `alpha` is

```text
w_(t-B)w_B/w_t.                                    (4.3)
```

Summing the marked child mixture multiplies (4.3) by (4.2), proving the
deep line of (1.1).  If `t<B`, the right-spine suffix cannot fit in the
last branch, giving the first line of (1.1).

## 5. Exact bounded falsification and scope

`closed_mean_formula.py` compares (1.1) with every exact contextual mean
through ambient `r=7`.  The computation may refute (1.1) but cannot prove
it.  The universal proof is the marked multiset deletion/insertion count
above.

The theorem removes the unknown contextual shape dependence from M56's
scalar problem.  It does **not** prove contextual quotient absorption:
the remaining obligation is the explicit weighted-composition inequality

```text
||H-E H||_(-1,R_s)^2
 <= E[phi 1_(last part=B)],                         (5.1)
```

with `H(C)` given by (1.1).  Nor does it solve M56's separate actual-edge
marked source-recovery problem.  It is therefore auxiliary and
nonterminal for both the parking projection and `K`.
# Audit of a global Rayleigh or cut lift

Date: 2026-08-12.  The exact scalar and marked-history obstructions below
do not presently give a slow mode for the full parking projection.

## 1. The synthetic mark is not a state observable

After one deep restriction, `(K,R)` records the total ordered attachment
history retained from all ancestor and sibling levels.  Equation (2.2) of
`marked_context_inheritance.md` is a mixture over those histories.  Two
different histories can reach the same unmarked last-branch macro with
different synthetic `(K,R)` values and different positional weights.

Consequently neither the bad scalar coefficient nor the event
`R=K-1` defines a subset of `J_s`.  A function of the unmarked plane tree
cannot simply read the synthetic context.  Summing history-specific Green
optimizers can create cross terms on every actual edge; this is exactly the
unresolved marked source-recovery problem from M56.

## 2. The literal ambient-fibre cut has polynomial escape

There is a genuine ambient realization of the extreme family.  For local
rank `s`, take ambient rank `r=s+K` and root composition

```text
b=(s+1,1,...,1)                 (K parts),          (2.1)
```

with the large branch leftmost, so `R=K-1`.  Its exact stationary mass is

```text
rho_r(b)=w_(s+1)/(K! Z_r).                          (2.2)
```

This realizes the contextual rates, but a cut supported inside this exact
root-composition fibre is not a superpolynomial bottleneck.  At every state
of the fibre, each of its `K-1` root child boundaries merges at total rate
`alpha_r K`, and the destination leaves the fibre.  Therefore every
`A subset F_b` satisfies

```text
Q(A,A^c)/pi(A)
 >=alpha_r K(K-1)
 =2K(K-1)/[3r(r-1)].                               (2.3)
```

For fixed `K` this is order `r^-2`, and for varying feasible `K<=r` it is
still inverse polynomial whenever nonzero.  Adding a nested unary-spine
condition inside `F_b` does not remove the root escape (2.3).

The stationary weight of a strict depth-`d` unary history also contains
the exact factor

```text
[K/(K+d)] [w_(s-d)/w_s],
```

which is exponentially small when `d` is proportional to `s`.  Thus the
most literal nested corridor has neither a closed boundary nor a
nonnegligible stationary side.

## 3. Why no Rayleigh upper bound follows

The local number

```text
||H-EH||_(-1,G_s)^2
```

is a dual energy for routing a conditional-rate charge on the accepted
root quotient.  It is not the variance of a recursively defined full-tree
observable.  Turning the local dual optimizers into a primal global test
requires extending them across neighbouring root-composition fibres to
avoid (2.3), while assigning one value to every unmarked state reached by
many marked histories.  No such consistent extension is currently known.

The first missing lift is:

> **UNMARKED NESTED-RAYLEIGH CONSISTENCY.**  Construct a real function on
> unmarked parking macros whose conditional martingale increments realize
> the marked contextual Green optimizers, with recoverable history
> collisions and with all root-merge/split edge energy accounted for.  To
> prove slow mixing, its variance/energy ratio must be superpolynomial; to
> rescue the comparison, the corresponding marked demand operator must
> instead have polynomial Green growth.

Absent this lift, the M65 results rigorously refute the scalar
disintegration template but neither upper-bound nor lower-bound the full
`Pbar_r` gap beyond inherited results.  There is also no stationary-flow
lift from this synthetic marked family to the fixed-endpoint bridge or the
original identity chain `K`; it cannot support Terminal B.

