# Exact additive-flow recurrence and its first missing coefficient

Date: 2026-08-11.  This note uses the full nonlazy parking projection
`Pbar_s`, its stationary law `pi_s`, and

```text
alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)].
```

It concerns only the minimal long-cycle sector, not the original identity
bridge chain `K`.

## 1. A contextual demand and its root filtration

Fix one contextual suffix-cut observable supplied by the universal locality
theorem, and normalize it as

```text
f=alpha_s phi >=0,       q=E_(pi_s) f.
```

The fixed suffix size is `B`.  For a root composition
`C=(c_1,...,c_k)`, put `h(C)=E[f|C]` and split the composition space into

```text
Z={C:c_k<B},  T={C:c_k=B},  D={C:c_k>B}.
```

Recursive contextual locality proves:

- `f=0` on every `Z` fibre;
- `f=h(C)` is constant on every `T` fibre;
- on a `D` fibre, `f` depends only on the standardized last-branch
  macro and is another contextual suffix-cut observable.

Define the exact deep-continuation fraction

```text
delta(f)=E[f 1_D]/q.                                 (1.1)
```

## 2. Telescoping of the internal recursive demand

Fix `C in D`, let `t=c_k-1<s` be the number of internal edges in its
last branch, and write the induced lower-rank contextual observable as
`f_t=alpha_t phi_t`.  The constrained-shuffle normalization and the
product restriction give the same coefficient

```text
gamma_(s,t)=t(t-1)/[s(s-1)]=alpha_s/alpha_t,
f=gamma_(s,t) f_t,
E_C=gamma_(s,t) E_(Pbar_t)+other nonnegative coordinates.   (2.1)
```

Suppose a lower-rank flow routes
`pi_t(f_t-Ef_t)` with energy at most `T_t E f_t`.  Scale that flow by
`gamma_(s,t)` and embed it in the last coordinate.  Its demand is exactly
`pi(.|C)(f-h(C))), while its conditional energy is

```text
gamma_(s,t)^2/[gamma_(s,t)] T_t E f_t
 =T_t h(C).                                         (2.2)
```

After multiplying by `rho_s(C)` and summing over `D`, all internal
recursive demands therefore cost at most

```text
delta(f) q max_(t<s) T_t.                           (2.3)
```

There is no Radon--Nikodym loss in (2.3).  Along active sizes
`s=s_0>s_1>...>s_j`, both the demand and capacity coefficients telescope:

```text
product_i gamma_(s_(i-1),s_i)
 =s_j(s_j-1)/[s(s-1)]=alpha_s/alpha_(s_j).          (2.4)
```

## 3. Exact quotient disintegration coefficient

Let `R_s` be the accepted stationary-flow root-composition quotient and
`Q_R(C,C')=rho_s(C)R_s(C,C')`.  Route the mean charge

```text
rho_s(C)(h(C)-q)
```

by a quotient electrical flow `theta`.  Put

```text
a(f)=(1/q) sum_e theta_e^2/Q_R(e)
    =||h-q||_(-1,R_s)^2/q.                          (3.1)
```

For one quotient edge `e=(A,B)`, disintegrate `theta_e` over the actual
fine crossing edges in proportion to stationary flow.  If `A` is the
refined composition and `B` the coarse one, the fixed merge boundary has
constant pointwise rate on `A`.  Thus the refined endpoint is exactly
`pi(.|A)`.  At a coarse state `x`, the endpoint density is

```text
p_e(x)/q_e,   p_e(x)=Pbar_s(x,F_A),
q_e=E_(pi(.|B))p_e,
```

and the residual fine demand is exactly

```text
theta_e pi(x|B)[p_e(x)/q_e-1].                      (3.2)
```

The contextual locality and norm-cancellation theorem turns (3.2) into a
strictly lower-rank contextual demand.  If its normalized flow cost is at
most `T_<s`, scaling its base flow gives energy exactly

```text
T_<s theta_e^2/Q_R(e).                              (3.3)
```

Hence, in the marked network in which residual commodities belonging to
different quotient edges have separate capacity copies, (2.3) and
(3.1)--(3.3) give the exact recurrence

```text
T_s(f) <= a(f)+[delta(f)+a(f)] max_(t<s)T_t.         (3.4)
```

This derivation retains all factors `rho(B)`, `q_e`, `gamma`, and
`alpha`; in particular, (3.3) is neither `T theta_e/q_e` nor
`T theta_e^2/q_e^2`.

## 4. The sufficient scalar absorption inequality

The scalar estimate

```text
a(f)<=1-delta(f)                                    (4.1)
```

would make the recursive coefficient in (3.4) at most one.  If the marked
commodities can also be projected to actual capacities without a
multiplicative collision loss, then

```text
T_s<=1+max_(t<s)T_t<=s.                             (4.2)
```

Thus every individual split coefficient would be at most `s`; summing
over at most `r` one-split refinements would prove M54's H-minus bound
with a fixed polynomial.  M41 Section 11 and M50's balanced induction would
then give an inverse-polynomial gap for the full parking projection.

The exact scalar proposition is:

> **CONTEXTUAL QUOTIENT ABSORPTION.**  For every contextual suffix-cut
> observable produced by constrained-shuffle disintegration,
> ```text
> ||E[f|root composition]-Ef||_(-1,R_s)^2
>   <= E[f 1_{last root branch size = B}].
> ```
> The right side equals `q(1-delta(f))` because the observable vanishes
> when the last branch is smaller than `B`.

This has not been proved.  Applying only the accepted quotient gap gives
`a(f)<=3e Var(h)/q`, which does not compare sharply enough with the
terminal mass and would multiply a constant once per spine depth.

## 5. The separate capacity-collision obligation

Even (4.1) is not alone sufficient.  Equations (3.3)--(3.4) add the
energies of edge-labelled residual commodities.  In the actual unmarked
chain, recursively routed commodities can share an internal edge.  The
inequality

```text
(sum_j F_j(e))^2/Q(e) <= sum_j F_j(e)^2/Q(e)
```

is false without cancellation or disjointness.  A crude Cauchy bound by
the number of contexts introduces a factor as large as `s` at every
depth and destroys (4.2).

The exact remaining flow proposition is therefore:

> **MARKED ADDITIVE SOURCE RECOVERY.**  Choose the quotient flows and their
> recursively disintegrated contextual flows so that each actual fine edge
> can recover its active-depth/root-boundary history with total squared
> load bounded by the right side of (3.4), up to one universal polynomial
> added over all depths, not multiplied at every depth.

Root-composition martingale differences at different active depths use
rotations at different vertices, so a depth mark is a plausible recovery
key.  No universal injection or fractional collision bound has yet been
proved.

## 6. Exact bounded falsification

`contextual_macro_energy.py` computes `a(f)`, `delta(f)`, and their
sum for every ambient split context through `r=7`.  There is no quotient
nullspace failure.  The largest observed values of
`delta(f)+a(f)` are

```text
ambient r       3        4        5        6        7
maximum       .5278    .6667    .7569    .8178    .8634
```

(the last displayed decimal is rounded upward; the stored value is about
`.8633184`).  The largest observed ratio
`a(f)/(1-delta(f))` is about `.382884`.  Thus (4.1) survives this
bounded falsifier with slack.  These floating electrical solves are finite
diagnostics only; they prove neither (4.1) nor the source-recovery claim.

The smallest open implication is CONTEXTUAL QUOTIENT ABSORPTION.  After it,
MARKED ADDITIVE SOURCE RECOVERY is still required before (4.2) is a proof
for the actual chain.
# M71 halfway checkpoint: the exact marked DAG survives, rank-only weights do not

Date: 2026-08-12.  Base commit:
`502a6f031c6d5a4bc0064ee5b370a4fa3914f993`.

## Scope and normalization

This mission concerns only the full nonlazy stationary-flow
parking-degree projection `Pbar_s` in the minimal long-cycle sector.  It
does not concern the identity bridge chain `K`.  Permutations compose as
`(pq)(x)=p(q(x))`; factors multiply left-to-right.

Write

```text
G_s=R_s/alpha_s,                 alpha_s=2/[3s(s-1)],
rho_s(C)=Z_s^(-1) [1/k!] product_i w_(c_i),
w_t=t^(t-1)/t!,                 C=(c_1,...,c_k).
```

For a contextual mark `x=(s,K,R,B)`, let `Phi_x` be M65's normalized
suffix statistic, `H_x(C)=E[Phi_x|C]`, and

```text
q_x=E H_x=w_(s+1-B)w_B/w_(s+1).
```

## H-001: exact child-mark-resolved Green DAG (proved accounting identity)

Let `theta_x` be the electrical root-quotient flow for
`rho_s(H_x-q_x)`.  For an undirected quotient edge `e`, orient its
refined endpoint as

```text
a=(...,A,B,...),        b=(...,A+B,...).
```

If `a` has `k` parts and the split boundary is `p` (zero based), the
residual contextual child has the exact mark

```text
y_e=(A+B-1, k-1, k-p-2, B).                         (H.1)
```

Its coefficient is

```text
[theta_x(e)^2/Q_G(e)]/q_x.                          (H.2)
```

On a deep root-composition group with `k` parts and last part `t>B`,
M65 marked inheritance gives children

```text
y_(k,t,j)=(t-1,K+k,R+j,B),        1<=j<=k,          (H.3)
```

with coefficients

```text
[rho_s(k,t) q_(t-1,B)/q_x]
  nu_(K,R,k)(j),                                    (H.4)

nu_(K,R,k)(j)
 =binom(R+j,j)binom(K-R-1+k-j,k-j)/binom(K+k,k).
```

Here `rho_s(k,t)` is the stationary mass of all compositions with
`k` parts and last part `t`, and
`q_(t-1,B)=w_(t-B)w_B/w_t`.  All children in (H.1) and (H.3) have
strictly smaller local rank than `s`.

Consequently, in M56's marked separated-capacity network, the exact
rank-resolved recurrence is

```text
T_x <= a_x
 +sum_(k,t>B,j) Wdeep(x,y_(k,t,j)) T_y
 +sum_e Wquot(x,y_e) T_y,                           (H.5)

a_x=||H_x-q_x||_(-1,G_s)^2/q_x.
```

The deep coefficients sum exactly to M56's `delta(x)`; the quotient
coefficients sum exactly to `a_x`.  Thus replacing all child values by
`max_(u<s)T_u` recovers M56's refuted scalar recurrence, while (H.5)
retains precisely the information lost there.  Equations (H.1)--(H.5)
follow by combining M56's exact electrical disintegration and
`alpha/gamma` cancellation with M65's pointwise marked inheritance.
No asymptotic or numerical input is used in this accounting identity.

## H-002: every rank-only polynomial Lyapunov weight fails (proved)

Fix an exponent `p>=0`.  A tempting repair assumes
`T_y<=C(rank(y))^p` in (H.5).  This cannot contract universally.

Take

```text
x_(s,K)=(s,K,K-1,s-1),       s>=2.
```

Only `C_0=(s)` is deep and only `C_1=(1,s-1)` is terminal.  Put

```text
h_s=w_(s-1)/w_s,
rho_0=rho_s((s))=w_s/w_(s+1),
lambda_s=sum_(A=1)^(s-1)w_Aw_(s-A)/w_s=2(s-1)/s.
```

The closed mean formula gives

```text
H(C_0)=h_s K/(K+1),       H(C_1)=2/(K+1),
q_x=rho_0 h_s,
deep mass/q_x=K/(K+1).                              (H.6)
```

Every quotient edge incident to `C_0` has residual child rank `s-1`.
The electrical demand at `C_0` is

```text
q_x[K/(K+1)-rho_0].
```

Its total incident conductance is `rho_0 lambda_s`.  Cauchy--Schwarz
for the incident electrical currents therefore forces rank-weighted
quotient energy at least

```text
q_x (s-1)^p
 h_s[K/(K+1)-rho_0]^2/lambda_s.                    (H.7)
```

Combining (H.6)--(H.7), the proposed weighted recursive coefficient is at
least

```text
(1-1/s)^p [
 K/(K+1)
 +h_s[K/(K+1)-rho_0]^2/lambda_s].                  (H.8)
```

Choose, for example, `K=s^2`.  Stirling gives

```text
h_s -> e^-1,       rho_0 -> e^-1,       lambda_s ->2,
```

so the lower limit of (H.8) is

```text
1 + e^-1(1-e^-1)^2/2 > 1.                          (H.9)
```

Hence every fixed rank power eventually amplifies.  This is an infinite
obstruction to a **rank-only proof template**, not a gap upper bound:
the child mark has suffix size `B=s-1` and becomes terminal after the
descent.  Forgetting `B` is exactly the false step.

## H-003: exact finite marked resolvent (empirical falsifier)

`marked_resolvent_probe.py` evaluates (H.5) recursively with every
`(K,R,B)` mark retained.  The rank DAG is finite because every child has
smaller rank.  Through `s=10`, scanning every `1<=K<=32`, every
`0<=R<K`, every `B`, and additional
`K=64,128,256,1024,4096` slices, the largest separated-capacity
resolvent values are

```text
s          2      3      4      5      6      7      8      9     10
max T   .444   .580   .671   .744   .790   .828   .857   .879   .898
```

The worst tested contexts have `K=4096,R=0` and moderate `B`.
The maximum deep-mass identity error is at floating linear-solve scale,
and the CG residuals are recorded in
`marked_resolvent_s10_k32.json`.  These values are compatible with

```text
T_x <=1-c/s
```

for a universal `c>0`, but are finite falsification evidence only.

`weighted_green_probe.py` separately confirms why coarse substitutes
are misleading.  Rank-only weights are headed toward the proved failure
(H.9).  A suffix-excess-only potential fails first on terminal hub
contexts, whose quotient disintegration creates nonterminal child marks.

## H-004: Schur complement and actual-edge collision

Let `A=I-Pbar_s` and split the Hilbert space into root-composition means
`M` and within-fibre fluctuations `Z`.  The exact root-mean energy
after harmonic relaxation is

```text
S=A_MM-A_MZ A_ZZ^dagger A_ZM.                       (H.10)
```

Positivity gives the qualitative contraction
`A_MZ A_ZZ^dagger A_ZM<=A_MM`.  The useful target is the quantitative
form

```text
A_MZ A_ZZ^dagger A_ZM
 <=(1-s^(-C))A_MM.                                  (H.11)
```

The finite marked values suggest an `s^-1` slack.  However (H.5) lives
in a network with history-separated capacity copies.  Different synthetic
histories can reach the same unmarked macro and actual edge.  Neither
(H.5) nor the finite `T_x<1` checks prove (H.11), because projecting
marked currents can create uncontrolled cross terms.

M70's full-twist theorem controls every nonzero cyclic character sector.
For a `U`-invariant test function, averaging (H.10) over all cyclic root
choices is therefore a plausible place for the history collisions to
cancel.  The parking macro is not deterministically conjugation-lumpable
(accepted M46), so this must be done on factorization microstates or the
exact averaged stationary-flow kernel, not by cyclically rotating a
degree vector.

## Remaining standalone proposition

> **MARKED DAG SLACK AND UNMARKING.**  Prove a universal
> `T_x<=1-s^-C` bound for the exact child-mark DAG (H.5), and construct
> its currents on actual unmarked `Pbar` edges with only polynomial
> additive load.  Equivalently, prove (H.11).  In the `U`-invariant
> long-cycle sector it is enough to prove the cyclic-root-averaged version,
> since M70 already controls every nonzero character.

The first half is now a completely explicit weighted-composition/electrical
DAG.  The second half is the surviving history-collision problem.  No claim
here is Terminal A or Terminal B for the original chain.

